1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,757
<i>Theme park!</i>

2
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:09,926
<i>- It was so fun.</i>
<i>- I had a blast today.</i>

3
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:12,012
- Yeah.
- It was really fun.

4
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:14,806
- Seung-hyun, why don't you agree?
- Huh?

5
00:00:14,889 --> 00:00:16,975
- Did you not have fun?
- Of course, I did!

6
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:19,185
I'm so jealous of your Pingu bag.

7
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:21,604
HAN SU-JI
AN JEONG-EUN

8
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,111
- What a fun day.
- So funny.

9
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:29,821
It's so warm here.

10
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:34,492
But honestly, during today's date,

11
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:37,120
I couldn't look Hyuk-joon in the eyes.

12
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:39,914
You see, Tae-hoon was there too.

13
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:42,834
And I had no problem looking at Tae-hoon,
but looking Hyuk-joon in the eyes

14
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,045
was kind of scary.

15
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,005
I couldn't bring myself to do it.

16
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:51,342
In any case, that's a change for me

17
00:00:51,968 --> 00:00:55,513
because I didn't feel anything
like that around Jung-yun.

18
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,056
That's why I said he's my top pick.

19
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:01,186
But why do I feel like this
when he's so not my type?

20
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,148
I'm in trouble. Hyuk-joon might be
my final pick at this rate.

21
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:07,442
- Really?
- It's her first time admitting it.

22
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:10,695
I came clean to Hyuk-joon about the gift.

23
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,197
- What about it?
- That I gave it to him.

24
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,991
A MOMENT AGO

25
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,576
So, did you get the gift?

26
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:20,121
The gift? Oh, so it was from you.

27
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:23,124
I was so confused.

28
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,960
- I actually thought it was from Han-ju.
- Oh, right.

29
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:29,005
Jin-woo told me he got a gift from you.

30
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:32,634
So I thought my gift couldn't be from you.

31
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:35,887
You'd usually give it to just one guy.

32
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:38,139
But I really appreciate it.

33
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,850
Hyuk-joon thinks
gift-giving is a big deal.

34
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:43,853
Yeah, he was actually a bit annoyed
that she gave a gift

35
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:45,104
- to both of them.
- He was furious.

36
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:47,023
He wasn't just a bit annoyed.
He was outraged.

37
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:49,192
- Gifts are really important to him.
- Yes.

38
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:50,527
DAY 8
D-2 UNTIL FINAL SELECTION

39
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,904
- There are only two days left.
- Oh my gosh.

40
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:54,864
There isn't much time left at all.

41
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:57,742
Let's go to the <i>Noraebang</i>.

42
00:01:57,826 --> 00:02:00,036
Hyun-seo just keeps getting hurt.

43
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,746
She's feeling very frustrated.

44
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:07,085
You know how Hyuk-joon and I
went on a lot of dates at the start?

45
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,419
You went almost every day.

46
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:11,840
And then Hyuk-joon went

47
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,383
- on four three-way dates.
- Yeah, he did.

48
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:15,635
And yesterday, he said to me

49
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:21,850
that he had no idea
those other women were interested in him.

50
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:28,523
He said he wanted to give them a chance.

51
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:30,441
What? He said what?

52
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:33,403
Wait. Let me get this straight.

53
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:36,197
So when I heard that,

54
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:37,699
I was like, "What?"

55
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,828
And on the three-way dates,

56
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:45,832
I found out for the first time
that other women were interested in me.

57
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:48,209
And I felt like it wasn't fair

58
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:50,378
to rule them out completely,

59
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:51,838
- so, I--
- What?

60
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:55,925
You were doing it for <i>them</i>?

61
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:58,678
It's hard to understand him.

62
00:02:58,761 --> 00:02:59,637
That's what I'm saying.

63
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:04,100
- But I think--
- He must have really thought that.

64
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:07,270
He must have thought it at least once,
which is why he said it.

65
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:11,149
We don't just blurt out things
we've never thought about.

66
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:13,484
We don't say things out of nowhere.

67
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:17,947
I think his popularity
has kind of gone to his head.

68
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:20,909
Go and tell him right now

69
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:22,911
to pick you
if there's a one-on-one date today.

70
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:26,623
- That's twisting his arm.
- That's true.

71
00:03:26,706 --> 00:03:28,833
Whatever he chooses… This is how I see it.

72
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,252
It's not like we are already a couple.

73
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:32,170
No, you're not.

74
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:34,297
We're still getting to know each other.

75
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:37,050
So I don't want to force him
to do what I want.

76
00:03:39,093 --> 00:03:40,345
If he goes

77
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:43,431
on a date with someone else again today,

78
00:03:43,514 --> 00:03:46,100
I'll just move on and be done with it.

79
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:49,437
This really is the last chance.

80
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,981
What if he doesn't
pick Hyun-seo again today?

81
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:53,983
Oh, Hyuk-joon.

82
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:55,902
Please choose wisely today.

83
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:00,657
- We got a text.
- What is it?

84
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:01,991
- They got a text.
- Yeah.

85
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:04,285
"You will go on a secret date today."

86
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:07,664
"You will get a guaranteed one-on-one date
with the person you pick."

87
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:08,915
A GUARANTEED DATE
WITH ONE PERSON OF YOUR CHOICE

88
00:04:08,998 --> 00:04:11,584
- What?
- Oh, come on!

89
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:13,920
Can we not pick anyone?

90
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,589
"You don't need to pick anyone."

91
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,591
YOU DON'T NEED TO PICK ANYONE
IF YOU DON'T WANT TO GO ON A DATE

92
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:21,636
<i>I did hesitate a bit.</i>

93
00:04:21,719 --> 00:04:23,429
It's hard knowing
it doesn't have to be mutual.

94
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:26,349
- The person I pick might not pick me.
- Right.

95
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:28,935
I need to do it anyway.

96
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:32,313
<i>I didn't feel conflicted anymore.</i>

97
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:36,943
<i>In terms of my feelings,</i>

98
00:04:38,194 --> 00:04:40,154
I've pretty much made up my mind.

99
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:43,116
<i>So I felt like I had to go on a date</i>
<i>with this person.</i>

100
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:44,200
<i>That's why I chose her.</i>

101
00:04:46,744 --> 00:04:48,329
<i>For the first time,</i>

102
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:51,541
we were allowed
to choose not to go on a date.

103
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,961
<i>I gave it a lot of thought.</i>

104
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:57,755
Wow.

105
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:02,260
Whoever they go on a date with
will be a secret to everyone else.

106
00:05:02,343 --> 00:05:06,055
And they get a guaranteed
one-on-one date with their pick.

107
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,683
- It's an amazing chance.
- It's a great opportunity.

108
00:05:08,766 --> 00:05:10,518
But Hyuk-joon said

109
00:05:10,601 --> 00:05:14,647
he is sure of his feelings
for the first time.

110
00:05:14,731 --> 00:05:16,733
Who do you think he picked?

111
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:18,568
I think it's Hyun-seo.

112
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:19,610
- Hyun-seo?
- Yes.

113
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:21,696
When he spoke to her,
he remembered how cool she is.

114
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:23,489
- Right.
- He suddenly remembered.

115
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:25,491
But Su-ji's a possibility too, right?

116
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:28,161
Su-ji said she couldn't
look Hyuk-joon in the eye.

117
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:31,831
And Hyuk-joon must have felt
that kind of romantic tension too.

118
00:05:31,914 --> 00:05:33,499
- Maybe.
- You're right.

119
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,043
I think he could pick Su-ji.

120
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:40,131
<i>- Where is this? It's pretty.</i>
<i>- It looks like a pottery studio.</i>

121
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:42,175
<i>It's perfect for Su-ji.</i>

122
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:45,762
- Oh, it's Jae-seo.
- Jae-seo!

123
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:49,182
- There's only one person he would pick.
- No doubt about it.

124
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:55,354
- Hello.
- Hello.

125
00:05:57,356 --> 00:05:59,484
- Hello.
- Hello.

126
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:00,818
Don't you think

127
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:03,654
whenever you go on a date with me,
it's a weird activity?

128
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:04,781
Oh, you're right.

129
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,618
You knew I would pick you, didn't you?

130
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:11,370
Oh, I picked you too.

131
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:13,706
Really?

132
00:06:14,373 --> 00:06:15,416
<i>- What?</i>
<i>- Huh?</i>

133
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,542
Yeah.

134
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:17,919
<i>- What?</i>
<i>- What's going on?</i>

135
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:20,379
- What?
- Seo-yoon picked him?

136
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,923
- She picked him too?
- All of a sudden?

137
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:24,175
- I've suddenly got butterflies.
- What's going on?

138
00:06:27,011 --> 00:06:29,722
I've wanted to say something
to him since yesterday,

139
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:33,017
and I felt I had to say it today.

140
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:35,770
So I picked Jae-seo without hesitation.

141
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:39,148
<i>How great. They picked each other.</i>

142
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,858
<i>Oh, how great!</i>

143
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:44,737
<i>- Jae-seo's heart must be racing.</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

144
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:47,073
Did you go to the Post Office yesterday?

145
00:06:47,156 --> 00:06:50,076
No, I did think about it, but…

146
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:51,869
Did you?

147
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:53,496
Yeah, I did.

148
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:55,373
- Really?
- Yeah, and I wrote you

149
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:59,085
a letter saying I wanted to talk today.

150
00:06:59,168 --> 00:07:01,295
- Did you?
- Yes. I wrote you a letter,

151
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:05,383
and you seemed a bit under the weather,
so I also bought you some vitamins.

152
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:06,342
Oh, thank you.

153
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:08,010
Make sure to take them.

154
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,137
What on earth?

155
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,305
It took nine days
for her to show some interest back.

156
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:12,974
Really? Hang on.

157
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:14,684
LAST NIGHT

158
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:16,936
Dear. Jae-seo…

159
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:18,896
<i>I wrote in the letter,</i>

160
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:22,316
<i>"Let's definitely talk tomorrow."</i>

161
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:25,653
<i>And he seemed a bit unwell,</i>
<i>so I also got him some vitamins.</i>

162
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:30,408
So even if we didn't get
a one-on-one date today,

163
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:33,911
I would have still found
a way to talk to you.

164
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:40,668
Well…

165
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:46,966
Honestly, I don't really think
my feelings will change.

166
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:53,264
I don't mean just toward you,
but all the guys here.

167
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:56,767
I don't think I feel
romantically attracted to anyone.

168
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:57,685
Right.

169
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:01,522
Given how

170
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:05,485
I don't feel that kind
of attraction toward anyone

171
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:08,738
even when I'm
in a special set-up like this,

172
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:12,450
maybe I'm just not someone
who gets those kinds of feelings.

173
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:18,372
For me to keep spending time
worrying about this

174
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:21,375
and spend the rest of my time here
not being myself…

175
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:24,462
The weather's too nice for that,
and there are so many great sights.

176
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:27,798
So I plan to just enjoy
the rest of my time here.

177
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:28,883
Okay.

178
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:30,843
Oh, this is…

179
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:43,231
- Thanks for telling me.
- No problem.

180
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:46,400
I think

181
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:48,402
it makes perfect sense.

182
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:51,447
Because we live in a world

183
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:54,158
where we can be perfectly content
without being in a relationship.

184
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:55,826
- Right.
- So…

185
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,914
I don't think it's a problem.

186
00:08:59,997 --> 00:09:02,166
Thanks for saying that.

187
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:10,466
<i>Honestly, as I've grown</i>
<i>closer to Seo-yoon recently,</i>

188
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:14,220
my feelings have slowly grown
just naturally being around her.

189
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:19,642
But she told me very clearly
that she wasn't interested,

190
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:20,977
so now I…

191
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:23,521
I guess I need to start moving on.

192
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:25,022
That's where I'm at now.

193
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:27,483
<i>Will something like this</i>
<i>ever happen again?</i>

194
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:31,862
<i>I feel like it is</i>
<i>a once-in-a-lifetime experience.</i>

195
00:09:31,946 --> 00:09:35,116
<i>I even wondered</i>
<i>if I deserved to be this happy,</i>

196
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:36,617
<i>and I don't have any regrets.</i>

197
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:40,371
Even if I were to go back
to day one with this knowledge,

198
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:42,373
I would still pick Seo-yoon.

199
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:46,252
Oh my gosh.

200
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:51,424
I admire how he is
so in touch with his emotions.

201
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:52,466
Yeah.

202
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:55,636
It's so great how grounded Jae-seo is.

203
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,054
- Yes.
- He was very cool just now.

204
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:58,806
Yeah, it's such a shame.

205
00:09:58,889 --> 00:10:02,101
If only he had been just as laid-back

206
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:03,811
when he talked with her earlier,

207
00:10:03,894 --> 00:10:05,896
perhaps things would've
panned out differently.

208
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,816
He said that he would pick her again

209
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:10,943
even though it's been hard
and things didn't work out.

210
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,320
It's just so cool.

211
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:13,988
- He really is a sexy guy.
- Yes.

212
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:15,740
Kudos to you, Jae-seo!

213
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:17,783
Where is this?

214
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,702
Oh, I think it's a batting cage.

215
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:26,208
<i>- I think it's Soo-hyun.</i>
<i>- I think it's her.</i>

216
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:28,002
<i>It is her!</i>

217
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:30,755
How will things go
for the Blueberry Couple today?

218
00:10:33,215 --> 00:10:34,425
<i>- Tae-hoon?</i>
<i>- It must be him, right?</i>

219
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:36,302
<i>Is it Tae-hoon? Who is it?</i>

220
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:37,428
<i>It must be Tae-hoon.</i>

221
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,057
<i>- It's Hoon-tae.</i>
<i>- I knew it.</i>

222
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,391
<i>- "Hoon-tae"?</i>
<i>- It's him.</i>

223
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:45,019
<i>She's happy to see him.</i>

224
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:46,812
- Welcome.
<i>- She's in a good mood today.</i>

225
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:48,564
- Hello.
- Hello.

226
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:49,565
SECRET DATE
SOO-HYUN, TAE-HOON

227
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:51,692
- How does this work?
- I'm not sure.

228
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:53,110
This pair is also…

229
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:55,821
- They're moving at different paces.
- They're a bit out of sync.

230
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,823
- It's a bit touch and go.
- They need to talk it out.

231
00:10:58,407 --> 00:10:59,408
What should we do?

232
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:01,327
We need to make a bet.

233
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:03,037
- Sure.
- That goes without saying.

234
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,455
What shall we bet on?

235
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:08,501
How many coupons do you have left?

236
00:11:08,584 --> 00:11:09,460
- I have three.
- Three?

237
00:11:09,543 --> 00:11:11,170
Then, I'd better take one.

238
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:13,214
- Okay!
- I want to get a gift of my choice.

239
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:14,423
What about you?

240
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:15,549
What do you want to play for?

241
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:17,802
Make me the same thing you made today.

242
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:19,428
The strawberry banana smoothie? Okay.

243
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:21,680
Tae-hoon's a smoothie wizard.

244
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:23,557
- He's a fruit expert.
- "Smoothie wizard."

245
00:11:25,976 --> 00:11:27,895
I found this hard.
I don't get how to do this.

246
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:33,609
I can't do it.

247
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:38,364
<i>She hasn't gotten a single hit.</i>

248
00:11:38,447 --> 00:11:39,865
<i>It can be so embarrassing</i>

249
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:42,535
<i>- when the guy you like is watching.</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

250
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:44,203
<i>It's embarrassing for guys too.</i>

251
00:11:45,996 --> 00:11:47,456
I've definitely lost.

252
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,917
- This is great.
- Oh, man.

253
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,043
I'm going to count.

254
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:52,086
I'm ready.

255
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:53,671
I'll win no matter what.

256
00:11:57,883 --> 00:11:58,717
<i>He has great form.</i>

257
00:11:58,801 --> 00:12:00,469
<i>- I think he'll do well.</i>
<i>- It looks promising.</i>

258
00:12:02,721 --> 00:12:03,973
<i>He's good.</i>

259
00:12:04,765 --> 00:12:05,891
You've done this before, right?

260
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:07,309
- Right?
- No.

261
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:09,937
<i>Seems like he has.</i>

262
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:13,149
<i>- He's got some experience.</i>
- Oh, come on.

263
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,943
Soo-hyun looks impressed.

264
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:18,112
You must really want those vitamins.

265
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:23,742
<i>She's got butterflies.</i>

266
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,995
<i>- Look at her. She's hiding her smile.</i>
<i>- You're right.</i>

267
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:27,413
My smoothie…

268
00:12:27,496 --> 00:12:30,249
- The smoothie store's closing.
- Oh, no. Why?

269
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:31,375
- He won't make any more for her?
- Score!

270
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:32,793
He says he's quitting.

271
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:35,212
He said he won't make her
any more smoothies.

272
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,381
- Wanna drink something?
- Yeah.

273
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:39,175
What do you want to drink?

274
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:41,010
Oh, are you buying?

275
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:42,303
Aren't we going Dutch?

276
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:43,512
This one? Jetty?

277
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,267
- Got it.
- Pass it over.

278
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:49,727
We should have bet on this.

279
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:51,103
No way.

280
00:12:51,729 --> 00:12:53,147
What a dopamine rush.

281
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,109
One of my three coupons…

282
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,236
You have to be ruthless
when it comes to things like this.

283
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,405
I can't just let you win.
You'll get spoiled.

284
00:13:03,407 --> 00:13:06,076
I've given you an honorable reason
to use the coupon.

285
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,203
I…

286
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:09,288
Darn it. I can't even speak.

287
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:12,166
Oh, man.

288
00:13:16,712 --> 00:13:19,632
So did you pick me? Or…

289
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:21,467
I'm not sure.

290
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,260
I don't know.

291
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,934
Oh, they don't know
whether they picked each other mutually.

292
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:32,603
I don't know. Why?

293
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:34,188
Why did you request… Who are you?

294
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,231
- What?
- Huh?

295
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:36,315
"Who are you?"

296
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,236
<i>Oh, he didn't pick her.</i>

297
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:41,237
SOO-HYUN REQUESTED THE DATE

298
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,614
So you might have another date later.

299
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,449
- Me? Maybe.
- Yeah.

300
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,118
What's wrong with him?

301
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,954
His tone could be a little hurtful.

302
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:53,207
<i>Judging by how Soo-hyun's looking unhappy…</i>

303
00:13:57,336 --> 00:13:58,212
Did you check it?

304
00:13:58,837 --> 00:13:59,713
Check what?

305
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,298
- Your cabinet.
- No, I didn't.

306
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,216
I haven't looked.

307
00:14:02,925 --> 00:14:04,510
Did you put something in it?

308
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:06,053
You didn't check it?

309
00:14:07,012 --> 00:14:08,430
Did you put something in there?

310
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,266
Okay. So whatever's in there is from you.

311
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:11,559
- You haven't looked at all?
- No.

312
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:13,018
What?

313
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:18,148
TWO DAYS AGO

314
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:24,989
<i>I worked up a lot of courage</i>
<i>to write him a letter.</i>

315
00:14:25,072 --> 00:14:26,907
<i>I said that I enjoyed the one-on-one date</i>

316
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:30,744
<i>and that I hoped we would get</i>
<i>another one-on-one date.</i>

317
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:32,872
All right. Here you go.

318
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:40,713
It's been two whole days.

319
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:43,340
If he was interested in her,
he would have checked it.

320
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:44,508
- Yes.
- Of course.

321
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,260
- Yeah.
- She must be upset.

322
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,596
You said you went regularly!

323
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:49,972
I haven't been once

324
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:52,016
since I… Because I'm done using it.

325
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,768
Honestly, after I put it in your cabinet,

326
00:14:54,852 --> 00:14:56,395
I kept watching to see how you reacted,

327
00:14:56,478 --> 00:14:58,147
but you didn't show any reaction at all.

328
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:01,317
And you seemed
like you had a lot on your mind.

329
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,360
So I wasn't sure if you saw it or not.

330
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:05,404
I wanted to ask you,
but I couldn't find you.

331
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:07,698
Why do you keep looking for me?
Stop looking.

332
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:12,786
I won't be going today, either.

333
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:13,704
What?

334
00:15:13,787 --> 00:15:15,873
Why won't he go
when she told him she left something?

335
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:18,792
I'm starting to get a bit annoyed.

336
00:15:19,793 --> 00:15:20,628
Why not?

337
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:22,212
Because I'm not using it right now.

338
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,423
But you might have gotten something.

339
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:25,466
Gotten something?

340
00:15:26,842 --> 00:15:28,427
I don't plan to go at all.

341
00:15:29,678 --> 00:15:31,639
Then you'll never know
if I'll give you the vitamins or not.

342
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:34,224
Put them in my cabinet and then tell me.

343
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:37,019
<i>Why is he taking it this far?</i>

344
00:15:40,981 --> 00:15:43,943
<i>Unfortunately, even though</i>
<i>I haven't read the letter yet,</i>

345
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,527
I know who it's from,

346
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:47,905
and I have some idea

347
00:15:47,988 --> 00:15:50,574
<i>of what it's probably about.</i>

348
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:54,244
But on my part,
in terms of romantic attraction,

349
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:57,122
I'm not as attracted
to Soo-hyun as she is to me.

350
00:15:57,206 --> 00:16:01,085
<i>So I'm trying to tell her indirectly</i>

351
00:16:01,168 --> 00:16:03,837
<i>that her interest in me</i>
<i>is making me a bit uncomfortable.</i>

352
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,633
Oh, come on.

353
00:16:07,716 --> 00:16:08,592
You can't do that.

354
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,803
Tae-hoon's being so rude right now.

355
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:12,471
- That's an awful attitude.
- Yeah.

356
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:14,139
He's being really rude.

357
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:15,557
- This is…
- "Rude."

358
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:16,475
It's rude.

359
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:18,310
- Don't you think so?
- It is a bit rude.

360
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:19,561
- He's being such a rude guy.
- It's…

361
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:21,480
It's just as In-guk said.

362
00:16:21,563 --> 00:16:23,315
- He summed it up nicely.
- Yeah, an awful attitude.

363
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:24,400
- It is.
- Totally awful.

364
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:25,734
He knows how she feels.

365
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:27,653
- That's what makes it so bad.
- Yeah.

366
00:16:27,736 --> 00:16:30,406
- He knows she requested this date.
- Exactly.

367
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:32,616
And this is how he behaves?

368
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,994
In Seo-yoon's case,

369
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:36,537
she was honest and straightforward.

370
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:38,789
- Yes.
- That's why Jae-seo

371
00:16:38,872 --> 00:16:41,125
- was able to take it so calmly.
- Yes.

372
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:43,919
- But the way Tae-hoon is acting right now…
- Yeah.

373
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,421
- It's hurtful.
- It is.

374
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:47,840
She must be wondering,
"How do I take this?"

375
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:50,092
- Yeah.
- It's just offensive.

376
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:52,761
The fact that he keeps smiling
makes it even worse.

377
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:54,054
- Exactly!
- Yes.

378
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:57,599
The way he's smiling
is bound to make her wonder,

379
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:00,477
"Is he kidding or is he messing me about?"

380
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:01,562
Exactly.

381
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:04,940
When I'm the one talking, it means
the participants aren't being problematic.

382
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:08,902
But if In-guk or Han-na speak up,

383
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:10,904
- it means they're doing terribly.
- It means it's serious.

384
00:17:10,988 --> 00:17:14,908
When I'm the one talking,
you can assume it's not so bad.

385
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:19,329
Do you not feel any…

386
00:17:19,413 --> 00:17:20,831
Do you not have any concerns?

387
00:17:20,914 --> 00:17:22,708
I did have one concern.

388
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:24,585
What was it?

389
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:26,754
Right now, I feel…

390
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:29,548
- Something's changed?
- There has been

391
00:17:29,631 --> 00:17:31,091
- a slight change.
- Slight?

392
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,927
My feelings have changed a bit.

393
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:38,766
I'm not sure what to do.

394
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:45,105
I see.

395
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:49,109
<i>It feels like Tae-hoon's changed a bit.</i>

396
00:17:49,193 --> 00:17:50,360
A lot, actually.

397
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,573
Do you think it might change?

398
00:17:54,656 --> 00:17:55,699
- Me?
- Yeah.

399
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,201
You mean my top pick?

400
00:17:58,786 --> 00:17:59,995
I'm talking to her right now.

401
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:02,623
- I'm talking to her.
- I'm very satisfied.

402
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:09,171
<i>I don't know.</i>

403
00:18:09,254 --> 00:18:13,258
When I was talking to Tae-hoon,
something felt a bit off.

404
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:16,512
But I can't put my finger on exactly what.

405
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:18,680
And I told him that I wrote him a letter,

406
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:21,934
but he said he hadn't seen it yet.

407
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:23,393
It made me wonder.

408
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:26,563
Does he just never go to the Post Office

409
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,315
or is he just not interested?

410
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,651
I felt upset for various reasons.

411
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:31,610
Of course, she did.

412
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:33,862
I'll see you back at the village.

413
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:35,114
- Bye.
- Bye!

414
00:18:40,869 --> 00:18:41,787
<i>Oh, dear.</i>

415
00:18:43,413 --> 00:18:45,582
It must be her first time
experiencing something like this.

416
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:48,752
- She must be taken aback. It's so sudden.
- Exactly.

417
00:18:48,836 --> 00:18:53,715
- She hardly asked him out or proposed.
- My point exactly.

418
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:55,759
She hasn't pushed him for anything.

419
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,636
But Tae-hoon's suddenly being
too mean to my Soo-hyun.

420
00:18:57,719 --> 00:19:00,222
She's the participant
I'm rooting for the most this season.

421
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:01,723
I was rooting
for the Blueberry Couple too.

422
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,559
It can feel a bit much for Tae-hoon

423
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:07,855
because she's acting like his girlfriend
and giving him so much attention.

424
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:09,314
- It might feel a bit early for that.
- Yeah.

425
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:10,357
That said,

426
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:14,194
instead of going about it
in such a hurtful way,

427
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:17,614
- it would've been nicer to just be honest.
- Exactly.

428
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:20,200
This is not good.

429
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:23,245
My heart breaks for her.

430
00:19:23,328 --> 00:19:24,913
Yeah, I'm worried she'll blame herself

431
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:27,207
- and wonder if she did something wrong.
- Exactly.

432
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:33,714
- Who's that?
- What?

433
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:35,799
- Was Soo-hyun picked
- It's another date.

434
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:36,884
- by someone else?
- Someone's coming.

435
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:38,760
<i>Who is it?</i>

436
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:42,306
<i>Seung-hyun?</i>

437
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:44,057
<i>- It's Seung-hyun!</i>
<i>- Oh, is it you, Seung-hyun?</i>

438
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:50,314
- Hi.
- Hello, sir.

439
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:54,234
Oh my.

440
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:55,986
Well done.

441
00:19:56,069 --> 00:19:56,987
- This is great.
- I love it.

442
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:59,615
Didn't Seung-hyun pick her
for the first impression vote?

443
00:19:59,698 --> 00:20:03,327
They were the only people
who picked each other.

444
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:05,579
- Hello.
- Welcome.

445
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:08,332
<i>Seung-hyun requested it.</i>

446
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:10,500
You got here first.

447
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,211
Yeah, I just… Yeah.

448
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:13,921
- You just got here?
- Yeah.

449
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,216
<i>I was so surprised.</i>

450
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:20,260
Seung-hyun hasn't
spoken to me much at all.

451
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,929
So when he showed up,

452
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:26,475
I was amazed and surprised
to get a chance to talk to him.

453
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:27,517
SECRET DATE
SEUNG-HYUN, SOO-HYUN

454
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:28,560
- So…
- Yeah?

455
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:31,230
I can't believe how nervous I am.

456
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:36,193
<i>Well, Su-ji was my top pick.</i>

457
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:39,738
And I was a bit upset
when she rejected me.

458
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:42,908
You asked if I thought my feelings for you

459
00:20:42,991 --> 00:20:45,577
might grow over time.

460
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:47,454
- Do you remember?
- Yeah.

461
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:49,539
I think that's unlikely.

462
00:20:49,623 --> 00:20:51,708
My mind's made up now.

463
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:53,752
They don't suit each other.

464
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:57,214
But after a few days,

465
00:20:57,297 --> 00:21:00,717
I started realizing it wasn't a big deal.

466
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:05,055
<i>And I thought I should pick</i>
<i>who I'm most interested in right now,</i>

467
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:09,726
<i>and Soo-hyun is the closest</i>
<i>to my ideal type, looks-wise.</i>

468
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:10,936
<i>Good thinking!</i>

469
00:21:11,019 --> 00:21:13,063
Honestly, I kind of…

470
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:18,568
I kind of want to talk
to Soo-hyun a bit more

471
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:20,696
- if I get the chance.
- Then, go get her.

472
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:22,030
But

473
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:24,116
things are going well
between her and Tae-hoon.

474
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:26,368
Just go for it.
What's there to be scared of?

475
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:28,578
We're here to throw caution to the wind.

476
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:29,496
- Did we?
<i>- She's right.</i>

477
00:21:29,579 --> 00:21:30,831
<i>- Yes.</i>
<i>- Well-said, Hyun-seo.</i>

478
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:34,001
I want to talk to Soo-hyun a bit more.

479
00:21:34,084 --> 00:21:35,210
Is that okay?

480
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:36,962
- You don't mind?
- No, I don't.

481
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:38,630
Who the heck is that?

482
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:40,257
Jeez.

483
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:42,551
- Such weird sunglasses too.
- So weird.

484
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:44,511
- What the heck?
- Why bother getting his permission?

485
00:21:44,594 --> 00:21:46,596
I thought to myself,

486
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:49,474
"Why didn't I do this before?"

487
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:51,977
I don't want any regrets,

488
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:55,105
so I wanted to talk to her
one-on-one before we left.

489
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:57,858
- It's our first time talking like this.
- Yeah, it is.

490
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:01,486
I actually wanted
to talk to you like this,

491
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:03,113
but the chance never came.

492
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:05,032
And to be honest,

493
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:06,658
I did think of trying to create a chance,

494
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:09,745
but I couldn't work up the courage.

495
00:22:09,828 --> 00:22:10,829
I see.

496
00:22:11,371 --> 00:22:14,082
So I feel lucky
that I got this chance today.

497
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:18,128
- I can't believe this took us so long.
- Yeah.

498
00:22:18,211 --> 00:22:20,380
He's mentioned her consistently!

499
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:21,965
They suit each other.

500
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:24,593
Did I tell you this?

501
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:26,386
What?

502
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,972
I picked you
for the first impression vote.

503
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:30,265
- Really?
- Yeah.

504
00:22:30,348 --> 00:22:32,142
- I picked you too.
- Really?

505
00:22:32,225 --> 00:22:34,102
You did? I had no idea.

506
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:36,813
Well, we haven't had a chance
to talk properly since then.

507
00:22:37,814 --> 00:22:39,399
- Yes.
- That's right.

508
00:22:39,483 --> 00:22:41,276
They picked each other.

509
00:22:41,359 --> 00:22:42,861
But they didn't know!

510
00:22:42,944 --> 00:22:44,821
It's day eight,
and they're only just finding out.

511
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:46,573
It took them eight days.

512
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:48,075
What a dramatic turn.

513
00:22:48,158 --> 00:22:50,285
- Gosh.
- Straight away on their first proper date…

514
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,748
<i>They must suddenly feel a bit giddy.</i>

515
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:58,794
- So…
- Yeah?

516
00:23:00,629 --> 00:23:02,089
What? What is it?

517
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:03,090
- Never mind.
- What?

518
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:11,098
What is it?

519
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:16,686
<i>I felt I should check how Soo-hyun felt</i>

520
00:23:16,770 --> 00:23:19,356
<i>before I expressed my feelings to her.</i>

521
00:23:20,148 --> 00:23:22,776
But I think I lacked the courage to ask.

522
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:25,028
It was nerve-racking

523
00:23:25,112 --> 00:23:27,989
- talking to someone I'm interested in.
<i>- Oh my.</i>

524
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:29,157
<i>This is great.</i>

525
00:23:30,408 --> 00:23:32,410
It's interesting that we're out here

526
00:23:33,203 --> 00:23:34,246
- talking like this.
- Yeah.

527
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:36,665
But honestly, I feel a bit regretful.

528
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:38,583
- About what?
- I wanted

529
00:23:39,209 --> 00:23:44,089
to work up the courage to say to you,
"Hey, do you want to talk?"

530
00:23:44,172 --> 00:23:45,006
You should have.

531
00:23:45,757 --> 00:23:48,677
Weren't we always
kind of around each other?

532
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:49,678
We were, but…

533
00:23:49,761 --> 00:23:50,971
I felt like…

534
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:53,932
If I said, "Hey, let's go and talk,"
it would be a bit…

535
00:23:54,015 --> 00:23:56,643
- Everyone would tease.
- Yeah, and the idea of that happening

536
00:23:56,726 --> 00:23:58,812
- just made me so shy.
- Right.

537
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:01,273
Actually, I get that.

538
00:24:01,356 --> 00:24:04,276
- What?
- Going up to someone and asking to talk

539
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:05,777
- isn't easy.
- No, it's not.

540
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:06,862
It's hard to be brave.

541
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:08,363
They seem at ease.

542
00:24:08,446 --> 00:24:09,614
They look good together.

543
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:10,991
It's so nice to see.

544
00:24:11,074 --> 00:24:13,535
And writing a letter is a bit…

545
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:15,954
- It feels a bit cheesy.
- Why not write a letter?

546
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:19,124
- I checked my cabinet so often.
- Really?

547
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:20,834
- Yeah. It's fine to write a letter.
- Yeah?

548
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:21,751
What's wrong with it?

549
00:24:23,086 --> 00:24:25,213
When I talk to someone,

550
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:27,465
it's not that I feel
awkward or uncomfortable,

551
00:24:27,549 --> 00:24:30,927
- but since I don't know them well,
- Yeah.

552
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:33,638
I don't know how to start a conversation,

553
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:35,724
and I'm worried I'll make a mistake.

554
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,142
- What kind of mistake?
- For example,

555
00:24:37,225 --> 00:24:39,895
what if I accidentally
say something that bothers them?

556
00:24:39,978 --> 00:24:42,606
But in any case,

557
00:24:42,689 --> 00:24:44,941
- we are, you know, talking right now.
- Yeah.

558
00:24:45,025 --> 00:24:48,445
And I feel like
you don't need to worry about that.

559
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:50,780
You shouldn't worry, and honestly…

560
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:54,951
During my makeover…
We can talk about this now, right?

561
00:24:55,702 --> 00:24:59,206
They taught me
how to be better at conversations

562
00:24:59,289 --> 00:25:00,457
and stuff like that.

563
00:25:00,540 --> 00:25:02,417
And my speech teacher taught me

564
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,794
about how to handle the fear

565
00:25:04,878 --> 00:25:07,422
of how the other person will react.

566
00:25:08,048 --> 00:25:10,592
They said it's unlikely
the other person will be insulted

567
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:13,178
as long as you express yourself clearly.

568
00:25:13,261 --> 00:25:15,847
And since it's unlikely,

569
00:25:15,931 --> 00:25:20,227
you shouldn't worry too much
about if you're being rude

570
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:22,520
- and just ask them.
- Really?

571
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:27,317
Even outside of this show,

572
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:30,028
you might keep

573
00:25:30,111 --> 00:25:32,530
facing this problem in the future,

574
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:36,076
so I think it would be good
for you to be less hesitant.

575
00:25:36,159 --> 00:25:38,161
Am I getting a makeover right now?

576
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:39,746
That's not what I'm trying to do.

577
00:25:39,829 --> 00:25:41,831
- Are you?
- I just mean if that was your concern…

578
00:25:41,915 --> 00:25:45,293
I just wanted
to share the advice I received.

579
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:47,212
I'm touched.

580
00:25:48,505 --> 00:25:50,548
You know, I think

581
00:25:51,049 --> 00:25:52,634
- that's a good way to think about it.
- Yeah.

582
00:25:52,717 --> 00:25:54,302
<i>Wow. This is so great.</i>

583
00:25:55,262 --> 00:25:57,097
What perfect timing.

584
00:25:57,180 --> 00:26:00,308
- Soo-hyun was a little hurt.
- Yes, she was.

585
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:01,851
- So it's--
- It's great timing.

586
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:04,104
It really could be the perfect timing.

587
00:26:04,187 --> 00:26:07,065
Speaking as a member
of Soo-hyun's fan club--

588
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,316
- You're in her fan club?
- Since when?

589
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,985
- You're her fan?
- You didn't know, did you?

590
00:26:10,068 --> 00:26:11,653
- No, we didn't.
- See here?

591
00:26:11,736 --> 00:26:12,612
You're a fanboy at heart?

592
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:15,699
When she first matched with Tae-hoon,

593
00:26:15,782 --> 00:26:17,909
she was excited that he picked her,

594
00:26:17,993 --> 00:26:19,703
so she spoke a mile a minute.

595
00:26:19,786 --> 00:26:20,829
But right now,

596
00:26:20,912 --> 00:26:23,039
she's not talking too fast.

597
00:26:23,123 --> 00:26:25,500
- She's calm.
- She's having a proper conversation

598
00:26:25,583 --> 00:26:26,835
- Yes.
- with Seung-hyun.

599
00:26:26,918 --> 00:26:28,336
I bet they're currently dating.

600
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:30,880
They even have the same initials!
They're both SH.

601
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:32,757
They can get matching initial necklaces.

602
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:34,301
- Yes.
- You know the ones.

603
00:26:34,384 --> 00:26:37,637
They can get SH stickers
on the back of their cars.

604
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:41,057
So, by any chance…

605
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:43,601
Have you made up your mind yet?

606
00:26:44,185 --> 00:26:47,772
I thought my mind was
pretty much made up, but…

607
00:26:48,857 --> 00:26:50,066
But something's changed?

608
00:26:50,150 --> 00:26:51,818
Yeah, it's changed a bit.

609
00:26:52,819 --> 00:26:55,447
I feel like I need
to give it some more thought.

610
00:26:58,033 --> 00:26:59,159
We need to explore all options.

611
00:26:59,242 --> 00:27:00,076
Yeah.

612
00:27:00,702 --> 00:27:02,454
- Let's do this.
- Let's do it.

613
00:27:02,537 --> 00:27:03,872
- Wow.
- Gosh.

614
00:27:03,955 --> 00:27:06,041
- Good. Let's go, SH.
- She just got butterflies.

615
00:27:06,124 --> 00:27:10,170
I feel like I've gotten used
to how things are here.

616
00:27:10,253 --> 00:27:11,963
- So--
- Me too. You seem very well-adapted.

617
00:27:12,047 --> 00:27:13,840
- Do I?
- Yeah.

618
00:27:13,923 --> 00:27:15,258
Your "mingle, single" on day one…

619
00:27:15,342 --> 00:27:17,093
- Oh, "Are you single? Let's mingle"?
- That dad joke.

620
00:27:17,177 --> 00:27:21,931
To be honest, Car, the garden
made me tell that joke.

621
00:27:22,515 --> 00:27:23,558
Did you ever use it again?

622
00:27:23,641 --> 00:27:25,560
- I mean--
- Huh? Should I use it on you now?

623
00:27:25,643 --> 00:27:26,978
- Are you going to?
- Right now?

624
00:27:27,062 --> 00:27:28,271
- Go on.
- Show her.

625
00:27:28,855 --> 00:27:30,482
Are you from Tasy?

626
00:27:30,565 --> 00:27:31,775
What?

627
00:27:33,109 --> 00:27:34,069
The land of fantasy.

628
00:27:38,823 --> 00:27:40,408
Success. That worked.

629
00:27:41,701 --> 00:27:43,078
It worked, didn't it?

630
00:27:43,912 --> 00:27:46,039
- What do you think? Not bad, right?
- Don't do it again.

631
00:27:46,122 --> 00:27:47,749
Throw that joke book away.

632
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:49,834
Why would you…

633
00:27:49,918 --> 00:27:51,503
- She told him to throw it away.
- She laughed.

634
00:27:51,586 --> 00:27:53,171
She enjoyed it. She's laughing.

635
00:27:53,254 --> 00:27:55,090
- It totally won her heart.
- It's like…

636
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:56,633
- It totally worked on her.
- It's like this.

637
00:27:56,716 --> 00:27:57,967
When she gets home, she'll think,

638
00:27:58,051 --> 00:27:59,344
- "That was so stupid." But then…
- Yes.

639
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:02,097
You get what I mean, right?

640
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:03,765
- You get it!
- The more you think about it,

641
00:28:03,848 --> 00:28:05,183
- the funnier it gets.
- It grows on you.

642
00:28:05,266 --> 00:28:06,851
- Yeah.
- "Are you from Tasy?"

643
00:28:06,935 --> 00:28:08,061
"The land of fantasy."

644
00:28:08,144 --> 00:28:10,480
Throw that joke book away.

645
00:28:10,563 --> 00:28:11,815
Why would you…

646
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:13,024
I read it this morning.

647
00:28:13,108 --> 00:28:14,484
Tell her a few more.

648
00:28:14,567 --> 00:28:17,278
- I thought, "This one's quite good."
- What's good about it?

649
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:19,531
What are you talking about?

650
00:28:22,117 --> 00:28:25,286
Seung-hyun is good at keeping
the conversation going,

651
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,746
and he's quite encouraging.

652
00:28:26,830 --> 00:28:28,623
Even though I was bad at baseball,

653
00:28:28,706 --> 00:28:31,459
he kept telling me I was doing a good job.

654
00:28:33,169 --> 00:28:34,379
I haven't hit a single one.

655
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:36,005
But it was a good effort!

656
00:28:39,050 --> 00:28:41,010
- Look, don't clap.
- Okay, I won't.

657
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:42,762
- I'll just stay still.
- I've missed them all.

658
00:28:42,846 --> 00:28:44,764
I thought, "I should have talked
to him sooner."

659
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:48,101
I found him more fun than I thought.

660
00:28:48,184 --> 00:28:50,061
This warms my heart.

661
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,980
Seung-hyun is so charming.

662
00:28:52,063 --> 00:28:54,649
He's way better than Tae-hoon,
who only cared about winning.

663
00:28:54,733 --> 00:28:56,359
- He is. Seriously.
- Yeah.

664
00:28:56,443 --> 00:28:58,445
Tae-hoon was acting like
he was on <i>Physical: 100</i>.

665
00:28:58,528 --> 00:29:02,741
At first, it seemed like Seung-hyun was
just on this show to have fun.

666
00:29:02,824 --> 00:29:06,661
- But he's being so sincere to Soo-hyun.
- Yeah.

667
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:08,163
His intentions seem so pure.

668
00:29:08,246 --> 00:29:09,789
- He's turned into a cool guy.
- He has.

669
00:29:09,873 --> 00:29:11,875
- They seem so compatible.
- They are.

670
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:13,251
I hope things work out between them.

671
00:29:13,334 --> 00:29:14,169
- Me too.
- Same.

672
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:16,796
Also, they're based in similar regions.

673
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:19,257
If not, just move, Seung-hyun.
I'll find you a place!

674
00:29:24,429 --> 00:29:25,472
<i>- Who's this?</i>
<i>- Who is it?</i>

675
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:28,725
<i>- Su-ji.</i>
<i>- It's Su-ji.</i>

676
00:29:28,808 --> 00:29:31,060
<i>Why does she look so deeply troubled?</i>

677
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:33,480
<i>Su-ji, you look like</i>
<i>you have a lot on your mind.</i>

678
00:29:39,611 --> 00:29:40,862
Is it Hyuk-joon?

679
00:29:40,945 --> 00:29:41,988
- Or Jung-yun?
- Is it Jung-yun?

680
00:29:42,071 --> 00:29:43,031
Could it be Hyuk-joon?

681
00:29:43,656 --> 00:29:46,117
- Who is it?
- Hyuk-joon? Based on those long strides…

682
00:29:47,577 --> 00:29:48,953
Hey.

683
00:29:49,829 --> 00:29:51,372
- Hello.
<i>- It's Jung-yun.</i>

684
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:52,749
Want to sit?

685
00:29:52,832 --> 00:29:57,754
<i>I wanted to spend</i>
<i>a bit more time with Su-ji.</i>

686
00:29:57,837 --> 00:30:00,632
<i>So I picked her for the date.</i>

687
00:30:02,008 --> 00:30:04,677
<i>Yesterday,</i>

688
00:30:04,761 --> 00:30:09,390
Hyuk-joon and Jung-yun's ranks changed,

689
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:13,144
so I said Hyuk-joon
became my top pick.

690
00:30:13,228 --> 00:30:15,396
<i>Maybe because of that change,</i>

691
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:17,357
<i>I felt a bit conflicted.</i>

692
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:20,276
And I just wanted to leave it up to fate.

693
00:30:20,360 --> 00:30:23,363
<i>But Jung-yun requested a date,</i>

694
00:30:23,446 --> 00:30:24,405
<i>so I went to meet him.</i>

695
00:30:25,281 --> 00:30:26,574
Aren't you cold?

696
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:27,492
Not right now.

697
00:30:27,575 --> 00:30:29,869
<i>I guess Su-ji didn't pick him.</i>

698
00:30:30,453 --> 00:30:34,040
SECRET DATE
JUNG-YUN, SU-JI

699
00:30:34,958 --> 00:30:36,709
This must be the place.

700
00:30:36,793 --> 00:30:37,919
What's all this?

701
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:40,088
Hello.

702
00:30:40,171 --> 00:30:42,465
You'll be making Japanese sweets today.

703
00:30:42,549 --> 00:30:44,968
It's very similar to clay.

704
00:30:45,051 --> 00:30:46,261
This should be fun.

705
00:30:48,888 --> 00:30:50,431
This must be second nature to you.

706
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:51,349
Well…

707
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:54,227
<i>Su-ji is a ceramicist, after all.</i>

708
00:30:54,853 --> 00:30:56,604
Hey, you're really good at this.

709
00:30:57,105 --> 00:30:58,898
You should get into pottery.

710
00:30:58,982 --> 00:31:00,066
You're doing well yourself too.

711
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:01,818
You might be better at this than me.

712
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:10,368
Do you want to date someone
who's like a friend

713
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:13,288
or someone who makes you
nervous and excited?

714
00:31:13,913 --> 00:31:15,915
This is her dilemma right now.

715
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:17,792
It's so obviously about him and Hyuk-joon.

716
00:31:19,168 --> 00:31:21,421
I said that I wanted a partner

717
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:23,548
who is like a friend.

718
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:26,926
In my diary in the 5 Minute Library,

719
00:31:27,802 --> 00:31:30,847
<i>for the question about dating</i>
<i>someone older, younger, or the same age--</i>

720
00:31:30,930 --> 00:31:35,435
<i>Yeah, I noticed that you gave</i>
<i>a very detailed answer for each one.</i>

721
00:31:36,102 --> 00:31:39,480
You clearly gave it a lot of thought.

722
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:41,024
THEY'RE THE SAME AGE
BOTH WERE BORN IN 2000

723
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:43,985
That's why I said I prefer
someone of the same age.

724
00:31:45,111 --> 00:31:46,029
What about you?

725
00:31:51,492 --> 00:31:52,535
<i>What will she say?</i>

726
00:31:53,620 --> 00:31:55,872
I think you need to feel butterflies.

727
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:58,625
You know, feeling nervous and stuff.

728
00:32:02,795 --> 00:32:04,380
Because for me…

729
00:32:04,881 --> 00:32:06,007
Have I told you this?

730
00:32:06,090 --> 00:32:09,302
The last time I really liked someone
was in sixth grade.

731
00:32:09,385 --> 00:32:10,762
Really?

732
00:32:10,845 --> 00:32:13,723
I was head over heels for him.

733
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:18,436
So I got really nervous around him,
and I used to turn bright red.

734
00:32:18,519 --> 00:32:21,105
My heart used to pound so hard.

735
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:24,859
So that feeling of being nervous and giddy

736
00:32:24,943 --> 00:32:27,362
and wanting to impress the other person

737
00:32:27,445 --> 00:32:29,572
became my idea of love.

738
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:35,536
- Jung-yun must get what she's getting at.
- Don't you think he caught on?

739
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:37,872
- I think he did.
- He's surprisingly perceptive.

740
00:32:40,541 --> 00:32:43,419
Sixth grade… That's quite a long time ago.

741
00:32:45,171 --> 00:32:46,089
A long time ago.

742
00:32:46,881 --> 00:32:49,217
But it was such a major event in my life.

743
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:51,928
Sometimes, I feel like
I'm still stuck in that memory.

744
00:32:52,011 --> 00:32:53,096
So…

745
00:32:53,888 --> 00:32:56,933
I keep comparing everything to that.

746
00:33:07,151 --> 00:33:09,570
Now that there isn't much time left,

747
00:33:10,947 --> 00:33:12,448
if you feel like

748
00:33:13,324 --> 00:33:15,660
your mind is basically made up,

749
00:33:16,369 --> 00:33:18,663
will you express it

750
00:33:18,746 --> 00:33:20,832
in one way or another?

751
00:33:24,502 --> 00:33:25,628
Yeah, I think so.

752
00:33:27,296 --> 00:33:29,632
- I'd have to let the other person know.
- Yeah.

753
00:33:30,675 --> 00:33:34,303
Honestly, I want to run away from it all
since it's so uncomfortable.

754
00:33:34,387 --> 00:33:36,222
But then my life will be
the same as before.

755
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:37,724
So I don't want to do that.

756
00:33:42,145 --> 00:33:43,604
Sorry that I'm so…

757
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:47,442
- Why are you apologizing?
- I wish I could give you a clear answer.

758
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:50,278
I'm always so wishy-washy.

759
00:33:56,159 --> 00:34:00,204
<i>It is a little upsetting</i>

760
00:34:00,288 --> 00:34:02,915
<i>since she's one of the women</i>

761
00:34:02,999 --> 00:34:05,543
<i>I've talked to the most,</i>

762
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:08,337
<i>and we've spent a lot of time together,</i>

763
00:34:08,963 --> 00:34:10,840
<i>but she's still unsure.</i>

764
00:34:10,923 --> 00:34:13,384
<i>She hasn't made her mind up yet,</i>

765
00:34:13,468 --> 00:34:15,636
<i>and she told me that directly.</i>

766
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:17,597
<i>And it doesn't feel like</i>

767
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:20,808
<i>there have been any big changes.</i>

768
00:34:21,350 --> 00:34:25,104
I feel like there's a bit of a wall.

769
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:28,941
<i>There's an invisible wall between us.</i>

770
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:32,403
<i>And I hoped</i>

771
00:34:32,487 --> 00:34:33,946
to get a gift

772
00:34:35,031 --> 00:34:37,158
or a letter or something like that.

773
00:34:37,241 --> 00:34:39,410
<i>Just in case I got anything,</i>

774
00:34:39,494 --> 00:34:41,245
<i>I kept dropping by the Post Office, but…</i>

775
00:34:45,374 --> 00:34:46,959
Of course, there isn't anything.

776
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,629
<i>I haven't gotten anything.</i>

777
00:34:50,797 --> 00:34:51,756
Oh, dear.

778
00:34:52,757 --> 00:34:54,342
- The way he said that…
- Yeah.

779
00:34:57,386 --> 00:34:58,596
Of course, it's empty.

780
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:03,392
<i>I thought it would be nice</i>
<i>to get something from Su-ji.</i>

781
00:35:08,481 --> 00:35:09,941
<i>He checked almost every day.</i>

782
00:35:10,566 --> 00:35:12,860
THIS MORNING

783
00:35:21,702 --> 00:35:24,789
- He checked a lot but expected nothing.
- The way he said, "Of course, it's empty."

784
00:35:26,040 --> 00:35:27,333
At the end of the day,

785
00:35:27,416 --> 00:35:30,294
over the course of ten days,

786
00:35:30,378 --> 00:35:34,465
<i>I had to express my feelings</i>
<i>by working up courage.</i>

787
00:35:36,759 --> 00:35:38,845
<i>And I had to wait for a reaction.</i>

788
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:42,348
So, I…

789
00:35:43,224 --> 00:35:45,226
expressed my feelings
and am waiting for a response.

790
00:35:46,185 --> 00:35:47,145
I do feel a bit…

791
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:50,481
It is a bit tiring.

792
00:35:51,023 --> 00:35:52,108
But

793
00:35:52,900 --> 00:35:56,571
feeling conflicted
and having so much on your mind

794
00:35:56,654 --> 00:35:59,949
<i>is toughest on the person</i>
<i>going through it.</i>

795
00:36:01,075 --> 00:36:05,580
So all I can do is wait and see.

796
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:12,336
It's so heartbreaking.

797
00:36:12,420 --> 00:36:14,797
- Yeah.
- The fact that he said to himself,

798
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:16,048
- "Of course, it's empty."
- Exactly.

799
00:36:16,132 --> 00:36:19,218
He got his hopes up, and that was his way

800
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:21,721
- of comforting himself.
- Yeah.

801
00:36:21,804 --> 00:36:23,598
But given the way Su-ji's acting,

802
00:36:23,681 --> 00:36:26,142
- it doesn't seem like she cut him off.
- No.

803
00:36:26,225 --> 00:36:27,602
I wonder what she's thinking.

804
00:36:27,685 --> 00:36:31,480
Is she still interested in him,
or does she feel too bad

805
00:36:31,564 --> 00:36:33,733
to reject him? It's hard to tell.

806
00:36:35,943 --> 00:36:36,819
<i>Who's this?</i>

807
00:36:39,488 --> 00:36:41,282
<i>- Jin-woo.</i>
<i>- It's Jin-woo.</i>

808
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:45,494
<i>- He probably picked Jeong-eun.</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

809
00:36:45,578 --> 00:36:47,955
<i>I think so too. But maybe not?</i>

810
00:36:50,416 --> 00:36:51,500
<i>It must be Jeong-eun, right?</i>

811
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:55,129
Hi.

812
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,839
It's an outdoor date.

813
00:36:56,923 --> 00:36:58,132
<i>It is Jeong-eun.</i>

814
00:36:58,758 --> 00:36:59,634
JIN-WOO REQUESTED THE DATE

815
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:01,260
<i>- Jin-woo requested it.</i>
- You must be cold.

816
00:37:04,805 --> 00:37:06,432
- It's a big spread.
- Right?

817
00:37:06,515 --> 00:37:08,768
- I didn't expect it to be so fancy.
- Yeah.

818
00:37:09,769 --> 00:37:12,021
It looks so tasty now that it's cooked.

819
00:37:12,104 --> 00:37:13,064
Let's give it a taste.

820
00:37:13,147 --> 00:37:15,483
- Thanks for grilling.
- Sure.

821
00:37:16,776 --> 00:37:17,985
- Careful. It's hot.
- Okay.

822
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:20,613
<i>- A camping date is so romantic.</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

823
00:37:21,364 --> 00:37:22,240
It's good.

824
00:37:27,328 --> 00:37:28,454
We're seeing each other a lot.

825
00:37:29,205 --> 00:37:30,748
It feels like I see you every day.

826
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:35,628
- We really don't have much time left.
- Right.

827
00:37:35,711 --> 00:37:37,922
- Tomorrow's basically the last day.
- It is.

828
00:37:38,756 --> 00:37:40,800
Are things going as you hoped?

829
00:37:40,883 --> 00:37:43,886
- Lately, I feel a bit…
- You're not too sure?

830
00:37:47,306 --> 00:37:48,182
Yeah.

831
00:37:49,392 --> 00:37:53,562
- It's not about you.
- Right.

832
00:37:53,646 --> 00:37:57,483
I just feel a bit confused
about my own mind.

833
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:02,530
- Jeong-eun was against dating a student.
- That's right.

834
00:38:02,613 --> 00:38:05,658
- Oh, that's right.
- She had crossed it off, but…

835
00:38:05,741 --> 00:38:08,494
- She had practical concerns.
- That's right.

836
00:38:08,577 --> 00:38:09,954
- It makes sense she's conflicted.
- Yeah.

837
00:38:12,456 --> 00:38:15,209
You do seem like
you have a lot on your mind.

838
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:18,379
But you feel quite sure
about your feelings, right?

839
00:38:18,462 --> 00:38:20,506
- Yeah, I feel pretty sure.
- Right?

840
00:38:20,589 --> 00:38:21,465
So…

841
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:24,719
I don't have any concerns left.

842
00:38:24,802 --> 00:38:26,637
And I envy that.

843
00:38:28,097 --> 00:38:32,435
When you have a lot of concerns,
it makes you hesitant.

844
00:38:32,518 --> 00:38:35,563
But now that my mind's made up,

845
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:37,857
even if I feel
a bit anxious about something,

846
00:38:38,357 --> 00:38:41,527
I'm like, "Let's just give it a try.
If it doesn't work out, oh well."

847
00:38:45,573 --> 00:38:48,492
I really appreciate that you are
willing to give me a chance,

848
00:38:48,576 --> 00:38:51,329
but I don't want you
to feel too pressured.

849
00:38:52,079 --> 00:38:55,291
Here's what I think.
When you tell someone you like them,

850
00:38:56,625 --> 00:38:58,753
on the surface,
it can seem like it's for them,

851
00:38:58,836 --> 00:39:01,464
but I think it's actually
a little bit selfish.

852
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:03,174
You do it because it makes you happy.

853
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:06,969
Of course, it'd be great if it's mutual.
I do hope you will like me back.

854
00:39:07,553 --> 00:39:11,140
But I appreciate you just hearing me out.

855
00:39:11,223 --> 00:39:12,767
So don't feel too pressured.

856
00:39:12,850 --> 00:39:13,726
Don't feel too…

857
00:39:14,643 --> 00:39:15,895
You shouldn't worry

858
00:39:16,645 --> 00:39:18,105
too much about it.

859
00:39:18,856 --> 00:39:20,608
Just enjoy yourself.

860
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:25,404
It's so sweet of Jin-woo
to relieve the pressure.

861
00:39:25,488 --> 00:39:27,490
Yeah, it's important to know
when to slow down.

862
00:39:31,327 --> 00:39:32,328
<i>To be honest,</i>

863
00:39:32,953 --> 00:39:35,164
<i>I obviously wish</i>
<i>she would feel the same way.</i>

864
00:39:35,247 --> 00:39:38,834
<i>I wish she was as sure as I am.</i>

865
00:39:38,918 --> 00:39:42,463
<i>But she seems like the type</i>
<i>who takes time to make up her mind.</i>

866
00:39:42,963 --> 00:39:46,509
<i>It's a shame that she seems</i>
<i>to be going back and forth.</i>

867
00:39:46,592 --> 00:39:49,720
It's like she's being
reluctantly pulled along.

868
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:50,971
Deep down,

869
00:39:51,597 --> 00:39:53,974
I was a bit disappointed.

870
00:39:59,522 --> 00:40:03,359
<i>I definitely like him</i>
<i>a lot more as a person,</i>

871
00:40:03,442 --> 00:40:06,529
<i>but I don't know</i>
<i>if my feelings are romantic.</i>

872
00:40:07,279 --> 00:40:10,825
Jin-woo's always been honest
about his interest in me.

873
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:14,703
I obviously appreciate that,
and it's a nice feeling.

874
00:40:14,787 --> 00:40:17,331
<i>But I feel like a student</i>
<i>and a working professional</i>

875
00:40:17,415 --> 00:40:20,126
<i>have too many different values,</i>

876
00:40:20,209 --> 00:40:23,462
<i>and I got the sense</i>
<i>that it would be hard to overcome that</i>

877
00:40:23,546 --> 00:40:25,881
<i>if we actually got together.</i>

878
00:40:25,965 --> 00:40:28,676
<i>And my feelings for him</i>

879
00:40:28,759 --> 00:40:30,886
<i>aren't strong enough to give it a go.</i>

880
00:40:33,764 --> 00:40:35,683
That changes things, doesn't it?

881
00:40:35,766 --> 00:40:38,352
- Yeah.
- It must be a big blocker for her.

882
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:40,354
Him being a student
and her being a working professional.

883
00:40:40,438 --> 00:40:42,606
And her feelings for him

884
00:40:42,690 --> 00:40:46,902
aren't strong enough to give it a shot
despite their differences.

885
00:40:46,986 --> 00:40:48,863
- She's not that into him.
- Not enough to look past it.

886
00:40:48,946 --> 00:40:50,698
Both Jeong-eun and Su-ji

887
00:40:50,781 --> 00:40:52,450
need to make up their minds now

888
00:40:52,533 --> 00:40:55,202
- and clearly express where they stand.
- Right.

889
00:40:56,620 --> 00:40:57,872
Whose date is this?

890
00:40:57,955 --> 00:40:58,831
Who is it?

891
00:41:01,125 --> 00:41:02,418
<i>Who's this?</i>

892
00:41:02,501 --> 00:41:04,378
<i>- Han-ju.</i>
<i>- It's Han-ju!</i>

893
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:09,633
<i>I was a bit torn.</i>

894
00:41:10,134 --> 00:41:11,969
HAN-JU'S THREE-WAY DATE

895
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:15,473
I've only been interested
in you two from the start.

896
00:41:16,599 --> 00:41:17,766
<i>She picked Jin-woo and Hyuk-joon.</i>

897
00:41:17,850 --> 00:41:19,310
<i>It must be one of them.</i>

898
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:23,272
<i>Looks-wise, her top pick</i>
<i>has always been Jin-woo.</i>

899
00:41:28,402 --> 00:41:31,113
<i>Jin-woo? Oh, Han-ju? Hyuk-joon?</i>

900
00:41:31,197 --> 00:41:32,364
<i>Who did she choose?</i>

901
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:36,660
<i>I wanted to talk</i>
<i>about different things with each of them.</i>

902
00:41:37,620 --> 00:41:39,121
<i>So it was hard to choose.</i>

903
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:47,963
- Hello.
- Hi.

904
00:41:50,299 --> 00:41:51,592
- Hello.
- Hi.

905
00:41:53,886 --> 00:41:56,222
SECRET DATE
HYUK-JOON, HAN-JU

906
00:41:56,305 --> 00:41:58,390
<i>She picked Hyuk-joon.</i>

907
00:42:02,019 --> 00:42:03,604
<i>Hyuk-joon said he was</i>

908
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:06,857
talking to several women
to get to know them.

909
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:09,485
But I figured his mind
must be made up by now,

910
00:42:09,568 --> 00:42:12,321
so I requested a date with him
to ask him where he stands.

911
00:42:12,404 --> 00:42:17,535
SECRET DATE
HAN-JU REQUESTED THE DATE

912
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:21,747
Did you expect this?

913
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:26,877
- A little bit.
- You had an inkling?

914
00:42:27,461 --> 00:42:30,214
What did you…
Did you come straight from the village?

915
00:42:30,297 --> 00:42:31,632
It's a secret.

916
00:42:31,715 --> 00:42:32,841
So you did.

917
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:35,427
Oh, man. This is…

918
00:42:37,638 --> 00:42:41,016
I feel like you may have done
the rounds today.

919
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:42,393
Not at all.

920
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:46,605
It's not like I can ask
since it's a secret.

921
00:42:50,192 --> 00:42:53,571
She must be curious
if he's made up his mind or not.

922
00:42:53,654 --> 00:42:56,240
That's why she requested the date,
so go on. Ask him.

923
00:42:57,992 --> 00:42:58,909
So what's the latest?

924
00:42:59,660 --> 00:43:04,081
You've spoken to most of the women now,
like you had planned.

925
00:43:04,164 --> 00:43:06,875
Have you made up your mind?

926
00:43:06,959 --> 00:43:08,002
My mind is…

927
00:43:09,628 --> 00:43:11,088
Yeah, I think I've decided.

928
00:43:12,881 --> 00:43:14,258
My mind is pretty much made up.

929
00:43:22,308 --> 00:43:25,019
I don't know if it's okay
to ask this so directly,

930
00:43:25,102 --> 00:43:26,395
but it's not me, is it?

931
00:43:33,819 --> 00:43:34,653
Wow, coming in hot.

932
00:43:38,157 --> 00:43:40,868
I think I'll feel better knowing.

933
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:43,412
I have an inkling,

934
00:43:44,330 --> 00:43:46,290
but I'd feel better if I knew for sure.

935
00:43:48,167 --> 00:43:50,586
- They need to decide today.
- They do.

936
00:43:50,669 --> 00:43:51,962
- That's right.
- It's time.

937
00:43:53,464 --> 00:43:55,257
You don't need to answer
if it's uncomfortable.

938
00:43:55,341 --> 00:43:57,635
No, I need to be honest
about these things.

939
00:43:57,718 --> 00:44:00,846
It makes sense that you want to know.

940
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:07,728
It is someone else.

941
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:09,730
I think I like someone else.

942
00:44:09,813 --> 00:44:10,981
I do like someone else.

943
00:44:15,527 --> 00:44:18,906
At least, Hyuk-joon's being honest
without leading her on.

944
00:44:20,032 --> 00:44:21,116
That said…

945
00:44:25,329 --> 00:44:28,040
You made the first move to talk to me,

946
00:44:28,123 --> 00:44:31,627
and you were so honest with me
during the ten-minute rotation date.

947
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:32,836
And your honesty

948
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:34,588
really made me

949
00:44:35,839 --> 00:44:37,091
feel drawn to you.

950
00:44:37,758 --> 00:44:40,552
I admired your honesty,
and I'm attracted to honest people.

951
00:44:40,636 --> 00:44:41,512
Right.

952
00:44:42,221 --> 00:44:46,100
You took the initiative…
And I really enjoyed our date yesterday.

953
00:44:46,183 --> 00:44:47,017
Yeah.

954
00:44:48,018 --> 00:44:49,895
I enjoyed all our conversations too.

955
00:44:52,231 --> 00:44:53,899
Gosh, you're so honest.

956
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:57,319
Well, actually…

957
00:44:57,403 --> 00:44:59,405
I've never been good
at opening up about my feelings,

958
00:44:59,488 --> 00:45:02,616
so I don't know how honest
I'm supposed to be.

959
00:45:02,699 --> 00:45:04,451
It's making me lay out all my cards

960
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:06,286
on the table.

961
00:45:07,871 --> 00:45:09,123
It has been

962
00:45:09,832 --> 00:45:11,500
a bit challenging and tough.

963
00:45:11,583 --> 00:45:13,877
But I came on this show
to try to open up more.

964
00:45:14,795 --> 00:45:16,422
That's why I applied.

965
00:45:17,631 --> 00:45:20,175
So I'm trying my best
even though it's embarrassing.

966
00:45:23,387 --> 00:45:24,346
Thank you.

967
00:45:26,306 --> 00:45:27,349
You're so admirable.

968
00:45:35,482 --> 00:45:38,902
<i>I felt like being clear and honest</i>
<i>was the respectful thing to do.</i>

969
00:45:39,486 --> 00:45:42,114
If I gave her a wishy-washy answer,

970
00:45:42,197 --> 00:45:43,365
she would have to

971
00:45:44,116 --> 00:45:45,951
<i>just keep waiting around.</i>

972
00:45:46,034 --> 00:45:48,245
<i>So I tried to be extra direct.</i>

973
00:45:52,374 --> 00:45:55,085
<i>As soon as I walked in,</i>

974
00:45:55,586 --> 00:45:57,921
I got him to confirm

975
00:45:58,005 --> 00:46:00,507
that his final selection

976
00:46:01,216 --> 00:46:02,259
isn't going to be me.

977
00:46:02,342 --> 00:46:04,219
I was a little embarrassed,

978
00:46:04,303 --> 00:46:06,597
but I didn't really feel
disappointed or anything.

979
00:46:07,181 --> 00:46:10,058
I would probably have been more hurt
if I'd had deeper feelings for him.

980
00:46:10,142 --> 00:46:15,230
<i>I'm just thankful that he made an effort</i>
<i>to get to know me. That's it.</i>

981
00:46:15,314 --> 00:46:17,191
- That's good.
- She's got high self-esteem.

982
00:46:17,274 --> 00:46:20,194
Have a drink and move on.

983
00:46:20,777 --> 00:46:22,738
I'm so curious what you girls talk about.

984
00:46:23,697 --> 00:46:25,782
We share everything.

985
00:46:25,866 --> 00:46:27,868
We really don't hold back.

986
00:46:29,953 --> 00:46:31,663
Don't get upset
when you watch the show later.

987
00:46:31,747 --> 00:46:34,166
- Did you badmouth me?
- Of course, we did.

988
00:46:36,084 --> 00:46:38,378
You looked so savage just then.

989
00:46:38,462 --> 00:46:41,840
I'm going to trash you so much
when I get back tonight.

990
00:46:44,051 --> 00:46:45,093
You're in for it.

991
00:46:46,512 --> 00:46:48,472
Talk smack all you want.
Trash him all night long.

992
00:46:49,431 --> 00:46:51,934
- Han-ju sounds like her old self now.
- Yeah, it's nice to see.

993
00:46:52,017 --> 00:46:53,769
They ended on a good note.

994
00:46:53,852 --> 00:46:55,020
- Yeah.
- It's nice.

995
00:46:55,103 --> 00:46:57,606
Hyuk-joon was so clear and upfront

996
00:46:57,689 --> 00:46:59,525
about the fact
that she isn't the one for him,

997
00:46:59,608 --> 00:47:02,152
so that closes the chapter on them.

998
00:47:02,236 --> 00:47:05,781
And luckily, it seems
he's finally done doing the rounds.

999
00:47:05,864 --> 00:47:06,698
- That's right.
- Yes.

1000
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:09,660
Han-ju said she used to struggle
with being honest,

1001
00:47:09,743 --> 00:47:13,705
but she's really grown
during her time in the village.

1002
00:47:13,789 --> 00:47:14,957
Yes, it's nice to see.

1003
00:47:15,040 --> 00:47:17,042
Han-ju will meet her one true love.

1004
00:47:17,125 --> 00:47:19,127
I can see her in a <i>gamjatang</i> place

1005
00:47:19,711 --> 00:47:22,965
ordering <i>gamjatang</i> for one
and a bottle of soju,

1006
00:47:23,048 --> 00:47:24,508
when suddenly a man across the room

1007
00:47:24,591 --> 00:47:27,970
also orders <i>gamjatang</i> for one
and a bottle of soju.

1008
00:47:28,053 --> 00:47:30,305
- And their eyes meet.
- And the serving lady says,

1009
00:47:30,389 --> 00:47:31,890
"Oh, sorry, dear."

1010
00:47:31,974 --> 00:47:33,684
"You'll have to sit together."

1011
00:47:35,185 --> 00:47:36,395
"Oh, sorry, dear."

1012
00:47:36,478 --> 00:47:38,855
- What a fun plot.
- That's exactly it!

1013
00:47:38,939 --> 00:47:40,357
So they'll shuffle to the same table.

1014
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:43,527
But then they realize,
"Hey, you're that rude bastard."

1015
00:47:44,778 --> 00:47:46,655
- It's perfect.
- I can see it.

1016
00:47:46,738 --> 00:47:49,074
I really hope something like that
will happen for her.

1017
00:47:51,201 --> 00:47:53,078
Hyuk-joon's already waiting
for his next date.

1018
00:47:53,161 --> 00:47:54,037
Hyun-seo?

1019
00:47:54,121 --> 00:47:56,748
I feel like Hyun-seo and Hyuk-joon
might get into a fight.

1020
00:47:58,792 --> 00:48:00,168
- Oh, no.
- No!

1021
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:01,420
- Don't do it!
- I can't watch this.

1022
00:48:01,503 --> 00:48:02,671
- Stop!
- Don't go on this date!

1023
00:48:02,754 --> 00:48:03,964
Don't do it.

1024
00:48:04,047 --> 00:48:05,799
- Don't go.
- I feel like this will be a disaster.

1025
00:48:05,882 --> 00:48:07,301
- I can't watch.
- Don't go on this date.

1026
00:48:09,469 --> 00:48:10,470
<i>I wonder who requested it.</i>

1027
00:48:10,554 --> 00:48:13,974
<i>- Maybe Hyuk-joon?</i>
<i>- Did Hyuk-joon request it?</i>

1028
00:48:16,685 --> 00:48:19,771
<i>Or maybe Hyun-seo requested it</i>
<i>to set things straight?</i>

1029
00:48:25,527 --> 00:48:26,528
Oh my gosh. I can't watch.

1030
00:48:27,696 --> 00:48:29,239
- Hello.
- Hi.

1031
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:36,330
SECRET DATE
HYUK-JOON, HYUN-SEO

1032
00:48:36,413 --> 00:48:38,498
- It's so sunny out.
- Yeah.

1033
00:48:42,878 --> 00:48:44,713
Who did you pick today?

1034
00:48:44,796 --> 00:48:47,049
Me? Who do you think?

1035
00:48:48,383 --> 00:48:49,926
I'm not sure.

1036
00:48:50,010 --> 00:48:51,011
Well, I…

1037
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:54,181
I just…

1038
00:48:55,641 --> 00:48:59,728
I got a letter requesting a date.

1039
00:48:59,811 --> 00:49:02,773
So I picked the person
who wrote the letter.

1040
00:49:02,856 --> 00:49:03,899
I see.

1041
00:49:04,524 --> 00:49:05,776
I wrote a letter yesterday.

1042
00:49:05,859 --> 00:49:07,527
Oh, look at them!

1043
00:49:08,153 --> 00:49:09,571
Good thing you read it.

1044
00:49:10,155 --> 00:49:12,032
Oh, he wrote her a letter.

1045
00:49:12,115 --> 00:49:14,493
THIS MORNING

1046
00:49:14,576 --> 00:49:16,161
<i>I found a letter in my cabinet.</i>

1047
00:49:16,244 --> 00:49:19,498
It was Hyuk-joon's handwriting.

1048
00:49:20,123 --> 00:49:23,543
<i>He said he wanted to go</i>
<i>on a date with me today.</i>

1049
00:49:24,169 --> 00:49:29,257
Since he took the initiative
to try to talk to me,

1050
00:49:29,341 --> 00:49:30,509
it made me think

1051
00:49:30,592 --> 00:49:32,928
I may have misunderstood him

1052
00:49:33,011 --> 00:49:35,555
by interpreting things only in my way.

1053
00:49:35,639 --> 00:49:38,475
<i>And I wanted to ask him</i>
<i>exactly what he was thinking</i>

1054
00:49:38,558 --> 00:49:39,893
<i>when he said what he said.</i>

1055
00:49:39,976 --> 00:49:41,395
<i>So it was mutual?</i>

1056
00:49:41,478 --> 00:49:43,271
<i>They picked each other.</i>

1057
00:49:45,565 --> 00:49:47,693
It's been a while

1058
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:49,069
- since we…
- Sat face-to-face.

1059
00:49:49,152 --> 00:49:50,153
Yeah, just the two of us.

1060
00:49:52,698 --> 00:49:57,703
Obviously, we didn't know
how the dates would be decided today,

1061
00:49:57,786 --> 00:50:00,706
but if you were to pick
someone else again today,

1062
00:50:00,789 --> 00:50:03,917
I was going to just move on.

1063
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:05,544
Really?

1064
00:50:06,169 --> 00:50:07,629
Because…

1065
00:50:07,713 --> 00:50:09,840
I don't know. To be honest…

1066
00:50:10,424 --> 00:50:12,926
You explained to me why

1067
00:50:13,009 --> 00:50:15,512
- you went on dates with other women.
- Yeah.

1068
00:50:17,305 --> 00:50:20,892
But your explanation
sounded a bit odd to me.

1069
00:50:21,393 --> 00:50:26,022
When you said
that you wanted to give a chance

1070
00:50:26,106 --> 00:50:28,483
to the women who were interested in you,

1071
00:50:28,567 --> 00:50:30,819
it made me raise my eyebrows a bit.

1072
00:50:30,902 --> 00:50:35,824
So, I wanted to ask
what exactly you meant by that.

1073
00:50:35,907 --> 00:50:38,201
Because it sounded to me like,

1074
00:50:39,244 --> 00:50:41,872
"I wasn't very interested in them,

1075
00:50:41,955 --> 00:50:44,624
but I gave it a go for their sake."

1076
00:50:44,708 --> 00:50:47,294
That's how it sounded to me.

1077
00:50:48,086 --> 00:50:49,546
It's hard to make sense of it.

1078
00:50:49,629 --> 00:50:51,798
Choose your words carefully, Hyuk-joon.

1079
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:55,343
What I actually meant was

1080
00:50:55,969 --> 00:50:56,970
that during the three-way dates,

1081
00:50:57,471 --> 00:51:00,056
the other women told me

1082
00:51:00,140 --> 00:51:02,017
that they were interested in me,

1083
00:51:02,100 --> 00:51:04,436
and when I thought about it,

1084
00:51:05,562 --> 00:51:09,107
I realized I had never
properly talked to them one-on-one.

1085
00:51:10,275 --> 00:51:13,236
So, I wanted to talk to them.

1086
00:51:15,280 --> 00:51:17,073
They said they were interested,

1087
00:51:17,157 --> 00:51:21,161
but I hadn't even considered
trying to open up to them.

1088
00:51:21,244 --> 00:51:22,329
So I wanted to try.

1089
00:51:23,330 --> 00:51:24,539
That's why I talked to them.

1090
00:51:24,623 --> 00:51:26,041
So you wanted that chance for yourself?

1091
00:51:26,124 --> 00:51:27,584
- That's it, right?
- Yeah, I needed it for me.

1092
00:51:27,667 --> 00:51:28,585
That's right.

1093
00:51:33,757 --> 00:51:36,134
That's a much clearer explanation.

1094
00:51:36,218 --> 00:51:38,053
Does it make sense now?

1095
00:51:38,136 --> 00:51:38,970
Yes.

1096
00:51:40,388 --> 00:51:41,723
So you misspoke?

1097
00:51:42,724 --> 00:51:43,558
Yeah.

1098
00:51:43,642 --> 00:51:46,102
Is that really what he meant,
but he just worded it wrong?

1099
00:51:46,186 --> 00:51:48,355
I wondered why you
never tried to come and talk to me.

1100
00:51:48,438 --> 00:51:49,439
- Because…
- Yeah?

1101
00:51:50,148 --> 00:51:51,233
To be honest,

1102
00:51:51,942 --> 00:51:55,529
if I were being my usual self,
I would have gone to you first.

1103
00:51:55,612 --> 00:52:00,200
I think I would have gone to you
and told you I wanted to talk.

1104
00:52:00,700 --> 00:52:02,410
And I made my feelings so obvious,

1105
00:52:02,494 --> 00:52:04,621
but I felt like I had to always

1106
00:52:04,704 --> 00:52:08,917
take charge and go up to you first.

1107
00:52:09,709 --> 00:52:11,837
And at the same time,

1108
00:52:11,920 --> 00:52:13,672
it seemed like you had a lot on your mind.

1109
00:52:13,755 --> 00:52:15,465
- So…
- That part is true.

1110
00:52:16,132 --> 00:52:19,511
I thought you might feel pressured
if I asked to talk to you.

1111
00:52:19,594 --> 00:52:21,805
So I just waited,
but it was quite frustrating.

1112
00:52:21,888 --> 00:52:25,725
So I kept wondering
when you'd come and talk to me.

1113
00:52:25,809 --> 00:52:28,854
But I appreciated you
asking to talk yesterday.

1114
00:52:30,188 --> 00:52:33,817
And I'm glad to be
on this date with you today.

1115
00:52:34,860 --> 00:52:36,486
<i>It felt like a load off my mind.</i>

1116
00:52:36,570 --> 00:52:39,281
I was so frustrated before,

1117
00:52:39,364 --> 00:52:40,824
so I felt relieved.

1118
00:52:40,907 --> 00:52:42,242
What?

1119
00:52:42,325 --> 00:52:43,243
What on earth?

1120
00:52:43,326 --> 00:52:46,538
That's it? She just… She seems happy.

1121
00:52:47,956 --> 00:52:50,625
- How was your date yesterday?
- At the theme park?

1122
00:52:51,626 --> 00:52:53,628
- I had so much fun.
- It seemed like it.

1123
00:52:54,254 --> 00:52:56,464
You were like, "We had so much fun!"
And you were all wearing

1124
00:52:56,548 --> 00:52:58,466
those Pingu bags, so I got a bit jealous.

1125
00:52:59,050 --> 00:53:00,760
- He was jealous?
- I thought,

1126
00:53:00,844 --> 00:53:04,222
"Do I need to buy a Pingu bag too?"

1127
00:53:04,890 --> 00:53:07,684
- Buy one sneakily to join the crew.
- I was honestly a bit jealous.

1128
00:53:07,767 --> 00:53:09,936
- It was my idea.
- I know.

1129
00:53:10,020 --> 00:53:11,521
I guess you were bothered.

1130
00:53:12,022 --> 00:53:13,023
Of course, I was.

1131
00:53:13,899 --> 00:53:17,402
So today, I didn't hesitate
even for a second.

1132
00:53:17,903 --> 00:53:19,195
I picked you instantly.

1133
00:53:19,279 --> 00:53:20,405
And last night,

1134
00:53:21,364 --> 00:53:22,198
you looked pretty, so…

1135
00:53:22,282 --> 00:53:23,742
Really?

1136
00:53:25,952 --> 00:53:29,789
<i>On my part, I used to have</i>
<i>a big weight on my mind</i>

1137
00:53:29,873 --> 00:53:31,875
because I had hoped Hyun-seo

1138
00:53:31,958 --> 00:53:36,880
would express her feelings
a bit more directly.

1139
00:53:36,963 --> 00:53:38,924
You really didn't get anything?

1140
00:53:39,007 --> 00:53:39,841
Me?

1141
00:53:40,842 --> 00:53:41,676
I'm not sure.

1142
00:53:41,760 --> 00:53:42,969
- You're not sure?
- No.

1143
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:44,512
- It's a secret.
- Oh, is it?

1144
00:53:45,138 --> 00:53:49,643
<i>So, in that respect,</i>
<i>I did feel a bit upset.</i>

1145
00:53:49,726 --> 00:53:52,020
<i>I was also torn</i>
<i>over shared interests versus fate.</i>

1146
00:53:52,562 --> 00:53:56,900
Then I realized that you can
enjoy activities even with your friends.

1147
00:53:57,609 --> 00:54:02,989
But someone being on your mind
and the feeling of missing them…

1148
00:54:03,740 --> 00:54:05,700
<i>That feels like fate.</i>

1149
00:54:08,954 --> 00:54:10,580
So you were sulking, Hyuk-joon?

1150
00:54:10,664 --> 00:54:11,665
I told you.

1151
00:54:11,748 --> 00:54:13,041
- That's it, right?
- He was upset.

1152
00:54:13,124 --> 00:54:15,293
Having similar hobbies and stuff
didn't matter, in the end.

1153
00:54:15,961 --> 00:54:17,420
He figured it out by doing the rounds.

1154
00:54:17,504 --> 00:54:19,172
- Hiking and whatnot didn't matter.
- Right.

1155
00:54:19,255 --> 00:54:20,507
What does this mean for Su-ji?

1156
00:54:21,049 --> 00:54:23,426
"I did the rounds,
and it turns out nothing beats fate."

1157
00:54:24,719 --> 00:54:26,012
Do you think

1158
00:54:27,097 --> 00:54:29,891
your mind is completely made up now?

1159
00:54:36,272 --> 00:54:37,607
I feel a bit embarrassed, but yeah.

1160
00:54:38,942 --> 00:54:40,443
<i>Gosh, he's sure.</i>

1161
00:54:40,527 --> 00:54:41,361
Good boy.

1162
00:54:45,156 --> 00:54:46,616
Since yesterday,

1163
00:54:47,450 --> 00:54:48,827
I've wanted to tell you,

1164
00:54:48,910 --> 00:54:50,578
"I did the rounds like you said,
and now I'm back."

1165
00:54:52,163 --> 00:54:53,832
I never told you to do the rounds.

1166
00:54:53,915 --> 00:54:56,001
You told me to talk to other women.

1167
00:54:56,084 --> 00:54:59,004
But did you need to go
on other dates to do that?

1168
00:54:59,629 --> 00:55:01,089
Yeah, she never told him to do the rounds.

1169
00:55:01,172 --> 00:55:02,882
Is there somewhere I can hide?

1170
00:55:02,966 --> 00:55:05,510
I just couldn't believe

1171
00:55:05,593 --> 00:55:09,055
that you wasted two chances
to pick me as your date.

1172
00:55:12,934 --> 00:55:15,812
It's honestly the first time in my life

1173
00:55:16,646 --> 00:55:19,149
I have ever waited for a guy.

1174
00:55:19,232 --> 00:55:20,984
You should be honored.

1175
00:55:21,067 --> 00:55:23,028
Of course, I am. It's a huge honor.

1176
00:55:23,111 --> 00:55:25,030
I'm not usually that kind of girl.

1177
00:55:25,530 --> 00:55:26,573
I'm honored.

1178
00:55:26,656 --> 00:55:27,741
- This is a thing.
- What's that?

1179
00:55:28,491 --> 00:55:29,409
It's an honor.

1180
00:55:29,492 --> 00:55:30,660
Where did you get that from?

1181
00:55:30,744 --> 00:55:33,830
Everyone kept saying, "Thank you,"
like that in the <i>Noraebang</i>.

1182
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:35,415
They bowed like this.

1183
00:55:36,416 --> 00:55:37,417
Yeah.

1184
00:55:37,500 --> 00:55:39,127
- Seo-yoon started it.
- Oh, really?

1185
00:55:39,210 --> 00:55:40,295
"It's an honor."

1186
00:55:41,504 --> 00:55:44,174
- It's not quite playing hard-to-get, but…
- Right?

1187
00:55:44,257 --> 00:55:46,009
It's like when a friend

1188
00:55:46,092 --> 00:55:48,344
you haven't seen in a while
comes to you crying

1189
00:55:48,428 --> 00:55:50,096
and complains about her boyfriend.

1190
00:55:50,180 --> 00:55:51,681
So you cuss him out,

1191
00:55:51,765 --> 00:55:54,100
but then the next day,
she's like, "We're back together."

1192
00:55:54,184 --> 00:55:55,393
- That's what it's like.
- Yeah.

1193
00:55:55,477 --> 00:55:58,480
- She is giving off that kind of vibe.
- Yeah, she is.

1194
00:55:58,563 --> 00:56:00,065
We were all a bit taken aback

1195
00:56:00,148 --> 00:56:03,234
because he was too attached
to Hyun-seo from the start.

1196
00:56:03,318 --> 00:56:06,821
- Right, but he turned cold overnight.
- That's right.

1197
00:56:08,323 --> 00:56:11,951
<i>I think he just chose his words wrong.</i>

1198
00:56:12,035 --> 00:56:13,703
When I asked him about it today,

1199
00:56:14,412 --> 00:56:17,582
he confirmed that he did
develop an interest in the others,

1200
00:56:17,665 --> 00:56:21,503
and he wanted to give himself
a chance to get to know them.

1201
00:56:21,586 --> 00:56:24,464
It's not that I completely understand,

1202
00:56:24,547 --> 00:56:28,760
<i>but I feel like he confirmed</i>
<i>his feelings for me on today's date.</i>

1203
00:56:28,843 --> 00:56:32,305
<i>So, I'll try to be</i>
<i>a bit less skeptical from now on.</i>

1204
00:56:32,388 --> 00:56:35,016
Judging by their faces,
it seems they've cleared the air.

1205
00:56:35,100 --> 00:56:37,018
As long as Hyun-seo's happy.

1206
00:56:37,102 --> 00:56:39,104
- That's all that matters.
- Yeah, exactly.

1207
00:56:39,187 --> 00:56:41,272
Just leave them be.

1208
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:43,274
They're happy, so leave them be.

1209
00:56:43,358 --> 00:56:46,236
<i>And to be honest,</i>
<i>I don't remember much else</i>

1210
00:56:46,319 --> 00:56:50,031
<i>other than him complimenting me</i>
<i>on how I styled myself yesterday.</i>

1211
00:56:50,115 --> 00:56:51,783
That was the most memorable moment.

1212
00:56:52,909 --> 00:56:54,828
Forget everything else.

1213
00:56:54,911 --> 00:56:57,330
There's nothing better
than being told you're pretty.

1214
00:56:57,413 --> 00:56:59,082
Hyun-seo is…

1215
00:56:59,999 --> 00:57:01,751
Just as I sensed from the start,

1216
00:57:01,835 --> 00:57:03,795
<i>her overall vibe is</i>

1217
00:57:03,878 --> 00:57:06,005
<i>the type of vibe I find attractive.</i>

1218
00:57:06,089 --> 00:57:09,801
<i>I've realized she is exactly my type.</i>

1219
00:57:09,884 --> 00:57:12,512
As for our date, just as I had expected,

1220
00:57:13,138 --> 00:57:14,264
I felt butterflies,

1221
00:57:14,347 --> 00:57:16,474
and I got excited when our eyes met.

1222
00:57:17,308 --> 00:57:19,602
I was sad the time passed so quickly.

1223
00:57:20,895 --> 00:57:22,063
He's really back to his old self.

1224
00:57:23,189 --> 00:57:25,900
The stairs are slippery, so be careful.

1225
00:57:25,984 --> 00:57:27,318
Okay.

1226
00:57:29,529 --> 00:57:32,323
- I feel like our outfits match.
- Do they?

1227
00:57:32,407 --> 00:57:34,200
We're both wearing a coat over a sweater.

1228
00:57:34,284 --> 00:57:35,160
- Uh oh.
- And we're both in black.

1229
00:57:36,578 --> 00:57:38,163
- You're right.
- They nearly held hands.

1230
00:57:38,246 --> 00:57:39,497
- Similar color tones and everything.
- Yeah.

1231
00:57:39,581 --> 00:57:41,499
- And it's not like we planned it.
- Right.

1232
00:57:42,459 --> 00:57:44,210
Hyun-seo should've grabbed his hand.

1233
00:57:45,420 --> 00:57:46,504
Just go for it?

1234
00:57:46,588 --> 00:57:49,507
And maybe Su-ji knows by now too.

1235
00:57:49,591 --> 00:57:53,595
Now that Hyuk-joon's requested
a date with someone else,

1236
00:57:53,678 --> 00:57:55,597
she'll figure out where he stands.

1237
00:57:55,680 --> 00:57:58,266
- So, what will Su-ji do now?
- Right.

1238
00:57:58,349 --> 00:58:01,478
- And what will Soo-hyun do?
- Exactly.

1239
00:58:01,561 --> 00:58:03,313
- That's the question.
- Let's keep watching.

1240
00:58:03,396 --> 00:58:05,690
Time is really running out now.

1241
00:58:08,526 --> 00:58:09,694
<i>Seo-yoon.</i>

1242
00:58:09,777 --> 00:58:11,404
<i>Hey! You're back!</i>

1243
00:58:11,488 --> 00:58:12,363
<i>Yeah.</i>

1244
00:58:12,447 --> 00:58:14,240
- This is--
- What do I do?

1245
00:58:14,324 --> 00:58:15,241
What's wrong?

1246
00:58:16,951 --> 00:58:19,037
- I think I'm going to cry.
- Why?

1247
00:58:19,120 --> 00:58:20,163
Why?

1248
00:58:20,246 --> 00:58:22,332
What's wrong, Soo-hyun?

1249
00:58:23,833 --> 00:58:24,667
I don't know.

1250
00:58:24,751 --> 00:58:25,668
Don't cry.

1251
00:58:25,752 --> 00:58:26,753
I'll give you a hug.

1252
00:58:28,171 --> 00:58:29,631
Who made you cry?

1253
00:58:33,051 --> 00:58:34,802
- Oh my gosh.
- Come here.

1254
00:58:34,886 --> 00:58:35,845
Don't cry.

1255
00:58:37,347 --> 00:58:39,474
On the date…

1256
00:58:39,557 --> 00:58:40,558
What is it?

1257
00:58:42,769 --> 00:58:44,229
- Don't cry.
- I don't know…

1258
00:58:49,275 --> 00:58:50,568
It's okay.

1259
00:58:52,612 --> 00:58:53,571
You're okay.

1260
00:58:54,864 --> 00:58:56,366
It's okay.

1261
00:58:56,449 --> 00:58:58,701
Lean on me until you're all cried out.

1262
00:59:02,789 --> 00:59:04,374
Don't cry.

1263
00:59:12,340 --> 00:59:14,467
<i>I was quite upset.</i>

1264
00:59:16,678 --> 00:59:20,223
I thought he would have picked me.

1265
00:59:20,306 --> 00:59:21,558
But he suddenly acted

1266
00:59:22,559 --> 00:59:25,186
like he had another date lined up

1267
00:59:25,270 --> 00:59:28,773
to get to know someone else.

1268
00:59:28,856 --> 00:59:32,694
<i>That's why I felt troubled.</i>

1269
00:59:34,571 --> 00:59:36,864
To be honest, I went
to give him the vitamins earlier.

1270
00:59:37,532 --> 00:59:39,826
- Don't tell me…
- Oh, because she lost the bet.

1271
00:59:39,909 --> 00:59:41,619
Those gummy vitamins are tasty.

1272
00:59:41,703 --> 00:59:42,954
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

1273
00:59:43,538 --> 00:59:45,707
But what if he still hasn't
taken the letter I left yesterday?

1274
00:59:45,790 --> 00:59:46,749
No way.

1275
00:59:46,833 --> 00:59:48,084
Take a look.

1276
00:59:48,167 --> 00:59:49,836
- Can I open someone else's cabinet?
- Yeah.

1277
00:59:51,254 --> 00:59:52,714
It's still in here.

1278
00:59:53,715 --> 00:59:54,966
Why won't he take it?

1279
00:59:55,925 --> 00:59:57,760
- Unbelievable. This is…
- That's so harsh.

1280
00:59:58,386 --> 00:59:59,262
Take it, Tae-hoon.

1281
00:59:59,345 --> 01:00:02,181
A letter is such a heartfelt gift.
How could he?

1282
01:00:03,433 --> 01:00:06,144
I did consider taking it back out,
but I'd already given it

1283
01:00:06,227 --> 01:00:07,478
and I already told him about it,

1284
01:00:07,562 --> 01:00:09,063
so he'd be flustered if it's gone.

1285
01:00:11,649 --> 01:00:12,775
Hang on.

1286
01:00:14,444 --> 01:00:15,278
Yeah.

1287
01:00:16,529 --> 01:00:18,531
Oh, man. I wasn't going to cry.

1288
01:00:27,290 --> 01:00:28,666
Hold on. This is driving me crazy.

1289
01:00:36,007 --> 01:00:37,342
I'm sorry. I need a minute.

1290
01:00:44,182 --> 01:00:45,141
Okay. I'll keep going.

1291
01:00:47,352 --> 01:00:48,186
Yeah.

1292
01:00:50,730 --> 01:00:52,023
Don't cry.

1293
01:00:52,732 --> 01:00:56,319
I'm trying my best to understand.
Maybe Tae-hoon was busy.

1294
01:00:56,402 --> 01:00:57,987
I'm trying to convince myself.

1295
01:00:58,071 --> 01:00:59,656
Busy doing what?

1296
01:01:01,157 --> 01:01:02,617
Right?

1297
01:01:02,700 --> 01:01:05,078
Oh, Soo-hyun. Don't cry.

1298
01:01:08,206 --> 01:01:09,123
Are you reading a book?

1299
01:01:09,999 --> 01:01:12,627
<i>She told me she wrote a letter.</i>

1300
01:01:12,710 --> 01:01:16,506
But she said she would
also buy me vitamins,

1301
01:01:16,589 --> 01:01:19,384
and I felt too lazy
to go to the Post Office twice.

1302
01:01:19,467 --> 01:01:21,844
So I gave her time to add the vitamins.

1303
01:01:24,097 --> 01:01:25,306
Stop smiling.

1304
01:01:25,390 --> 01:01:27,725
His smile makes you even more…

1305
01:01:27,809 --> 01:01:29,477
What's making me so mad…

1306
01:01:29,560 --> 01:01:32,021
- It makes you angrier.
- His smile is so unnatural.

1307
01:01:32,105 --> 01:01:34,315
He'll make a comment and then be like…

1308
01:01:35,775 --> 01:01:38,820
- That's right.
- He smiles after a beat.

1309
01:01:38,903 --> 01:01:40,363
"I gave her time."

1310
01:01:40,446 --> 01:01:42,156
This is what's so infuriating!

1311
01:01:42,240 --> 01:01:44,492
He's making me so angry.

1312
01:01:45,827 --> 01:01:46,703
<i>It's Seung-hyun.</i>

1313
01:01:58,005 --> 01:01:59,257
- Where are you going?
- Go!

1314
01:01:59,340 --> 01:02:00,675
- Where are you off to?
- Go to her!

1315
01:02:00,758 --> 01:02:01,592
- Please.
- Now's the time.

1316
01:02:01,676 --> 01:02:02,802
Let's go, SH!

1317
01:02:02,885 --> 01:02:04,053
Come on, SH couple!

1318
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:05,054
Go quickly!

1319
01:02:06,597 --> 01:02:11,644
NORAEBANG

1320
01:02:12,353 --> 01:02:13,730
I'm going to check out how I look.

1321
01:02:16,190 --> 01:02:17,150
Pull her aside!

1322
01:02:18,234 --> 01:02:20,486
- Where are you going?
- To look in the bathroom mirror…

1323
01:02:20,570 --> 01:02:21,571
- The bathroom?
- Yeah. Why?

1324
01:02:24,407 --> 01:02:25,783
- What's up?
- I wanted a quick chat.

1325
01:02:25,867 --> 01:02:27,285
- Okay.
- You don't mind?

1326
01:02:27,952 --> 01:02:28,995
Well done.

1327
01:02:29,078 --> 01:02:30,288
That's the stuff.

1328
01:02:30,830 --> 01:02:32,582
- Well done, Seung-hyun!
- Way to go!

1329
01:02:37,378 --> 01:02:38,629
<i>- He's shy.</i>
<i>- He's so shy right now.</i>

1330
01:02:38,713 --> 01:02:40,298
<i>He's feeling bashful.</i>

1331
01:02:42,633 --> 01:02:45,052
I'm not sure what to say. One sec.

1332
01:02:45,136 --> 01:02:46,304
I called you out, but…

1333
01:02:46,387 --> 01:02:47,889
No, it's okay. I'm enjoying the fresh air.

1334
01:02:47,972 --> 01:02:49,056
- The fresh air?
- Yeah.

1335
01:02:49,724 --> 01:02:50,767
I needed to cool off.

1336
01:02:50,850 --> 01:02:51,851
- Really?
- Yeah.

1337
01:02:53,978 --> 01:02:57,398
- Honestly, at the start… Well…
- Yeah?

1338
01:02:58,232 --> 01:03:02,153
- You know I kept having dates with Su-ji?
- Yeah.

1339
01:03:02,236 --> 01:03:03,654
After those dates,

1340
01:03:03,738 --> 01:03:08,534
I started to really develop
deep feelings for her.

1341
01:03:08,618 --> 01:03:09,786
- For Su-ji?
- Yeah.

1342
01:03:11,162 --> 01:03:12,246
But then…

1343
01:03:12,830 --> 01:03:15,374
She said she appreciated it

1344
01:03:15,458 --> 01:03:17,502
- but felt we were on different pages.
- It wasn't mutual.

1345
01:03:17,585 --> 01:03:19,545
- She said that?
- That's what she said.

1346
01:03:21,172 --> 01:03:23,257
- It kind of hurt.
- Of course!

1347
01:03:23,341 --> 01:03:25,676
- Of course, it hurt. You're only human.
- Yeah.

1348
01:03:25,760 --> 01:03:27,637
- So, it hurt.
- Yeah.

1349
01:03:28,638 --> 01:03:30,097
But after time passed,

1350
01:03:30,765 --> 01:03:32,600
I felt… I feel better.

1351
01:03:32,683 --> 01:03:33,518
So…

1352
01:03:34,393 --> 01:03:36,437
As I said before,

1353
01:03:37,188 --> 01:03:39,023
you've always been one of my picks.

1354
01:03:39,106 --> 01:03:40,358
- That's right.
- Yeah, so…

1355
01:03:41,108 --> 01:03:45,446
That's why I wanted to talk to you today.

1356
01:03:46,614 --> 01:03:47,448
And…

1357
01:03:51,536 --> 01:03:52,829
- What is it?
- I don't know.

1358
01:03:52,912 --> 01:03:55,832
Anyway, my interest in you right now is…

1359
01:03:55,915 --> 01:03:57,083
Are you saying you're interested?

1360
01:03:57,166 --> 01:03:58,918
- You're my top pick right now.
- Oh, your top pick.

1361
01:03:59,001 --> 01:04:00,628
But like… I…

1362
01:04:01,128 --> 01:04:03,047
I don't want to confuse you

1363
01:04:03,130 --> 01:04:05,883
because I know that you have
feelings for Tae-hoon.

1364
01:04:05,967 --> 01:04:07,677
I don't want to interfere.

1365
01:04:08,302 --> 01:04:11,222
I must seem like a bit of a wimp, but…

1366
01:04:11,305 --> 01:04:12,139
I just really…

1367
01:04:12,223 --> 01:04:13,266
I don't think you're a wimp.

1368
01:04:13,349 --> 01:04:15,101
- Really?
- A wimp wouldn't call me out like this.

1369
01:04:15,184 --> 01:04:16,519
- You think so?
- A wimp can't do that.

1370
01:04:16,602 --> 01:04:19,063
The real wimp
is reading a book in his room.

1371
01:04:20,398 --> 01:04:23,150
Anyway, don't feel pressured.
Just know that's how I feel.

1372
01:04:23,234 --> 01:04:26,112
I just wanted to let you know.

1373
01:04:26,195 --> 01:04:29,574
So you just wanted me to know
you're interested in me?

1374
01:04:30,908 --> 01:04:31,826
- Yeah.
- Okay.

1375
01:04:32,952 --> 01:04:33,870
Firstly, thank you.

1376
01:04:33,953 --> 01:04:36,247
- My pleasure. But honestly…
- Yeah?

1377
01:04:38,249 --> 01:04:40,668
I was so nervous before I went in.

1378
01:04:41,669 --> 01:04:43,421
- When you came in earlier?
- Yeah.

1379
01:04:43,504 --> 01:04:44,463
I was nervous and…

1380
01:04:45,047 --> 01:04:46,591
I also had butterflies.

1381
01:04:49,343 --> 01:04:51,262
Anyway, that's how I feel.

1382
01:04:51,345 --> 01:04:53,973
That's where I stand.

1383
01:04:54,849 --> 01:04:57,351
But how did you feel about our date today?

1384
01:04:58,603 --> 01:05:00,271
I was thankful.

1385
01:05:00,354 --> 01:05:01,814
I really appreciated it

1386
01:05:01,898 --> 01:05:03,941
because my top pick was also…

1387
01:05:04,025 --> 01:05:06,027
Not my top pick,
but for the first impression vote,

1388
01:05:06,110 --> 01:05:07,778
- I picked you too.
- Yeah.

1389
01:05:07,862 --> 01:05:09,864
I thought you seemed
like a really good guy.

1390
01:05:09,947 --> 01:05:11,574
I kept thinking to myself

1391
01:05:11,657 --> 01:05:15,912
that I would like to stay in touch
with you even after the show.

1392
01:05:17,872 --> 01:05:19,790
I'm glad that's how you saw me.

1393
01:05:22,043 --> 01:05:23,711
- Thank you for telling me.
- Yeah.

1394
01:05:23,794 --> 01:05:26,130
Honestly, I really appreciate it.

1395
01:05:26,756 --> 01:05:29,467
I had a lot on my mind and stuff,
but you've cheered me up.

1396
01:05:31,218 --> 01:05:32,470
Well, anyway…

1397
01:05:34,722 --> 01:05:35,932
Let's keep our chin up!

1398
01:05:36,015 --> 01:05:37,016
Yeah, let's stay strong!

1399
01:05:37,099 --> 01:05:38,392
- Thanks for telling me.
- Sure.

1400
01:05:38,476 --> 01:05:40,770
I'll give it some thought.

1401
01:05:41,395 --> 01:05:42,521
- I'll have a think.
- Okay.

1402
01:05:45,441 --> 01:05:46,442
- Thanks for telling me.
- Yeah.

1403
01:05:46,525 --> 01:05:47,360
Shall we get up now?

1404
01:05:47,443 --> 01:05:48,444
- Let's go.
- It's cold, right?

1405
01:05:48,527 --> 01:05:49,445
I'm not that cold.

1406
01:05:49,528 --> 01:05:50,571
- Really?
- I feel warmer now.

1407
01:05:50,655 --> 01:05:51,989
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

1408
01:05:52,990 --> 01:05:54,033
I feel so much lighter.

1409
01:05:54,116 --> 01:05:55,159
- Really?
- Yeah.

1410
01:05:55,242 --> 01:05:58,329
When I have something on my mind--

1411
01:05:58,412 --> 01:05:59,872
- You need to let it out?
- Yeah.

1412
01:05:59,956 --> 01:06:01,916
So I thought I'd try like this.

1413
01:06:04,210 --> 01:06:05,753
<i>I was honestly so grateful</i>

1414
01:06:05,836 --> 01:06:08,255
<i>because I was feeling depressed</i>
<i>about how Tae-hoon acted.</i>

1415
01:06:08,339 --> 01:06:11,592
That's why I cried.

1416
01:06:11,676 --> 01:06:15,262
So when Seung-hyun came
and told me all that,

1417
01:06:16,013 --> 01:06:18,057
I was so thankful.

1418
01:06:18,140 --> 01:06:20,851
<i>It made me want to talk to him more.</i>

1419
01:06:21,519 --> 01:06:24,689
I can't show her exactly what I'm feeling,

1420
01:06:24,772 --> 01:06:26,565
and I'm not sure
if I was fully successful,

1421
01:06:26,649 --> 01:06:28,901
but I think I managed
to convey my feelings to some degree.

1422
01:06:28,985 --> 01:06:31,487
She's my current top pick,

1423
01:06:31,570 --> 01:06:34,824
<i>so I'll keep trying my best</i>
<i>to impress her.</i>

1424
01:06:36,826 --> 01:06:39,078
- Just when she needed some comfort.
- Yeah.

1425
01:06:39,161 --> 01:06:40,663
Talk about perfect timing.

1426
01:06:40,746 --> 01:06:43,124
- He did great.
- It really cheered her up.

1427
01:06:43,207 --> 01:06:44,959
SH, don't cry.

1428
01:06:46,210 --> 01:06:48,254
- Don't cry.
- SH, don't cry.

1429
01:06:48,963 --> 01:06:50,798
- It's "either-or" questions.
- "Either-or."

1430
01:06:50,881 --> 01:06:51,924
I love it.

1431
01:06:52,008 --> 01:06:52,842
NORAEBANG

1432
01:06:52,925 --> 01:06:55,386
Shall we just go in order?

1433
01:06:55,469 --> 01:06:56,887
- Shall we?
- Yeah.

1434
01:06:56,971 --> 01:06:59,140
This is going to be challenging.

1435
01:07:00,808 --> 01:07:04,437
"What if your partner takes their coat off
for your friend on a cold day?"

1436
01:07:04,520 --> 01:07:05,438
That is f…

1437
01:07:05,521 --> 01:07:06,731
Freaking unacceptable.

1438
01:07:06,814 --> 01:07:08,274
Of course, it's unacceptable.

1439
01:07:08,357 --> 01:07:10,317
Han-ju nearly cursed.

1440
01:07:10,401 --> 01:07:12,236
I'd be cold too.

1441
01:07:12,319 --> 01:07:13,612
"I'd be cold too."

1442
01:07:14,196 --> 01:07:15,906
- Of course, it's not okay.
- Unacceptable.

1443
01:07:15,990 --> 01:07:17,116
Jung-yun, you're next.

1444
01:07:18,909 --> 01:07:20,953
"A partner who dated
just one person for ten years,

1445
01:07:21,037 --> 01:07:22,121
or someone who…"

1446
01:07:22,204 --> 01:07:23,289
- Gosh.
- I mean…

1447
01:07:23,372 --> 01:07:26,959
- 10 years?
- We haven't dated in 27 years.

1448
01:07:27,043 --> 01:07:28,669
This question isn't fair.

1449
01:07:28,753 --> 01:07:30,004
I think I prefer the former.

1450
01:07:30,087 --> 01:07:32,131
This one's a bit tricky.

1451
01:07:32,214 --> 01:07:33,257
It is tricky,

1452
01:07:33,340 --> 01:07:35,468
- but if I had to choose…
- Yeah.

1453
01:07:35,551 --> 01:07:36,719
What's this party of fun people?

1454
01:07:36,802 --> 01:07:38,471
I prefer the latter without a doubt.

1455
01:07:38,554 --> 01:07:39,847
- Really?
- Yeah.

1456
01:07:39,930 --> 01:07:42,767
But if they only dated
one person for ten years,

1457
01:07:42,850 --> 01:07:44,560
won't they keep thinking of their ex?

1458
01:07:44,643 --> 01:07:45,644
They're basically a divorcee.

1459
01:07:47,772 --> 01:07:49,190
She never holds back.

1460
01:07:51,942 --> 01:07:54,320
Do you want to join in?

1461
01:07:54,403 --> 01:07:55,863
No, keep going.

1462
01:07:55,946 --> 01:07:57,406
You all prefer the former?

1463
01:07:57,490 --> 01:07:58,365
Yeah. I prefer the former.

1464
01:07:58,449 --> 01:08:00,117
- That looks fun.
- Yeah, the former is a bit…

1465
01:08:00,701 --> 01:08:01,869
Go on. Pick one.

1466
01:08:03,913 --> 01:08:05,915
"Name a time when the person you like
made you upset."

1467
01:08:06,415 --> 01:08:10,086
The question is about the time
you've been upset by someone you like.

1468
01:08:12,838 --> 01:08:14,381
- She's right there listening.
- Yeah.

1469
01:08:14,465 --> 01:08:15,758
- By someone you like?
- Yeah.

1470
01:08:15,841 --> 01:08:18,594
- Be honest.
- It has to be someone in the village.

1471
01:08:19,303 --> 01:08:20,679
Of course.

1472
01:08:22,389 --> 01:08:24,642
Upset by someone…
What if you've never been upset?

1473
01:08:24,725 --> 01:08:25,559
Should I make it up?

1474
01:08:26,143 --> 01:08:27,645
You haven't been hurt? Not even once?

1475
01:08:27,728 --> 01:08:29,480
Cross your heart?

1476
01:08:29,563 --> 01:08:31,107
- Why did you cry, then?
- Yeah, why?

1477
01:08:31,690 --> 01:08:33,275
There has to be a reason.

1478
01:08:33,359 --> 01:08:35,027
Can I step out for a minute?

1479
01:08:35,736 --> 01:08:36,779
Do you feel awkward?

1480
01:08:40,116 --> 01:08:41,158
So you <i>have</i> been upset.

1481
01:08:41,242 --> 01:08:42,076
She's running away.

1482
01:08:42,159 --> 01:08:43,911
- Why are you running away?
- She's running.

1483
01:08:47,164 --> 01:08:50,626
I would like to get a clear answer

1484
01:08:51,335 --> 01:08:52,378
from that person.

1485
01:08:55,798 --> 01:08:56,715
Now.

1486
01:08:57,508 --> 01:08:59,385
- In that case…
- We forgot to put the used ones aside.

1487
01:08:59,468 --> 01:09:00,803
I didn't think we'd get to me.

1488
01:09:00,886 --> 01:09:01,971
But it doesn't matter, does it?

1489
01:09:02,555 --> 01:09:03,889
If you get the same question…

1490
01:09:03,973 --> 01:09:06,559
"Name a time when the person you like
made you upset."

1491
01:09:06,642 --> 01:09:08,853
- It's the same question.
- Here it is.

1492
01:09:08,936 --> 01:09:10,020
<i>It's the same thing again.</i>

1493
01:09:10,104 --> 01:09:11,939
When they didn't like me back.

1494
01:09:15,526 --> 01:09:16,819
That is upsetting for sure.

1495
01:09:16,902 --> 01:09:18,237
It is upsetting.

1496
01:09:18,946 --> 01:09:19,905
Let's stack it like this.

1497
01:09:21,991 --> 01:09:23,909
- They've all experienced that.
- Yeah.

1498
01:09:30,166 --> 01:09:32,376
<i>I was so busy thinking</i>
<i>about my own feelings.</i>

1499
01:09:32,459 --> 01:09:35,671
I only worried about the person
I was interested in

1500
01:09:35,754 --> 01:09:38,090
and what I should do about it,

1501
01:09:38,174 --> 01:09:40,176
so I didn't think much
about the people around me.

1502
01:09:40,259 --> 01:09:42,553
But now that I have
organized my thoughts a bit,

1503
01:09:42,636 --> 01:09:44,930
I have a bit more headspace
to think about other people.

1504
01:09:45,014 --> 01:09:46,182
As a result of that,

1505
01:09:46,265 --> 01:09:49,602
<i>I started noticing</i>
<i>Han-ju's expressions a bit more.</i>

1506
01:09:49,685 --> 01:09:51,770
<i>After all, she had told me</i>
<i>she was interested in me.</i>

1507
01:09:52,521 --> 01:09:55,649
And I started wondering
what kind of things have hurt her, so…

1508
01:10:01,447 --> 01:10:03,532
Han-ju, can we talk for a bit?

1509
01:10:03,616 --> 01:10:06,118
- Yeah.
- I'd better give you guys space.

1510
01:10:07,203 --> 01:10:10,873
Jin-woo asked Han-ju to talk.

1511
01:10:10,956 --> 01:10:12,208
Where shall we go?

1512
01:10:13,667 --> 01:10:15,252
The Garden?

1513
01:10:15,336 --> 01:10:16,462
I just need a minute.

1514
01:10:16,545 --> 01:10:17,379
Okay.

1515
01:10:17,463 --> 01:10:19,924
I wanted to talk to you too.

1516
01:10:21,425 --> 01:10:22,468
I feel like Han-ju

1517
01:10:23,302 --> 01:10:24,303
may have gotten butterflies.

1518
01:10:25,971 --> 01:10:29,016
I had a lot to say,
but now I don't know where to start.

1519
01:10:31,477 --> 01:10:33,854
I wanted to thank you, firstly,

1520
01:10:34,605 --> 01:10:36,941
since you picked me for the dates.

1521
01:10:38,567 --> 01:10:42,154
And I've been feeling a little guilty.

1522
01:10:43,822 --> 01:10:44,657
For me,

1523
01:10:45,282 --> 01:10:47,952
you made the best impression
on the first day.

1524
01:10:48,035 --> 01:10:51,121
Don't make me mad.
I cried because of that.

1525
01:10:51,914 --> 01:10:53,249
So why did you have to read mine?

1526
01:10:54,625 --> 01:10:56,168
There were so many other diaries.

1527
01:10:56,252 --> 01:10:58,212
But it's just that…

1528
01:10:58,295 --> 01:11:01,840
On our date, you said I made
a great first impression on you.

1529
01:11:01,924 --> 01:11:05,636
So I thought maybe you liked me back.

1530
01:11:06,262 --> 01:11:07,221
But then,

1531
01:11:07,304 --> 01:11:09,390
it turned out I wasn't
your first impression pick.

1532
01:11:09,473 --> 01:11:11,684
Yeah, her name wasn't in his diary.

1533
01:11:11,767 --> 01:11:14,103
He didn't mention her once.

1534
01:11:14,687 --> 01:11:17,314
I feel like you'll get angrier
if I keep talking, so I'll stay quiet.

1535
01:11:17,398 --> 01:11:19,233
Come out with it, quickly.

1536
01:11:19,316 --> 01:11:21,527
What is it? Spill it.
Let's get it all out.

1537
01:11:21,610 --> 01:11:23,028
- You really want to talk it all out?
- Yeah.

1538
01:11:23,112 --> 01:11:24,530
I swear it's not that I wasn't interested.

1539
01:11:24,613 --> 01:11:27,533
- You know I had a hard few days.
- Yeah.

1540
01:11:27,616 --> 01:11:29,451
I honestly felt really torn
during that time.

1541
01:11:29,952 --> 01:11:31,287
Don't give me bullshit.

1542
01:11:33,163 --> 01:11:34,623
She's right. Don't give her bullshit.

1543
01:11:35,708 --> 01:11:37,042
Han-ju just got some closure,

1544
01:11:37,126 --> 01:11:39,420
- so he shouldn't give her hope again
- Yeah.

1545
01:11:39,503 --> 01:11:42,256
- if he's not interested.
- Right, exactly.

1546
01:11:42,339 --> 01:11:43,507
- It's better to leave her be.
- Yes.

1547
01:11:43,590 --> 01:11:46,176
Honestly, I really
gave it a lot of thought.

1548
01:11:46,260 --> 01:11:47,761
It was such a tough time for me.

1549
01:11:47,845 --> 01:11:52,474
I thought,
"He said he was into three women."

1550
01:11:52,558 --> 01:11:55,102
"But I guess
I'm not even in the top three."

1551
01:11:55,185 --> 01:11:57,271
- So…
- I swear you're mistaken.

1552
01:11:57,896 --> 01:11:59,106
You were definitely one of them.

1553
01:11:59,189 --> 01:12:00,190
- Really?
- Yeah.

1554
01:12:00,274 --> 01:12:01,358
I swear.

1555
01:12:03,235 --> 01:12:04,445
But anyway,

1556
01:12:05,237 --> 01:12:07,406
do you not have any regrets
or things you wish you did?

1557
01:12:08,282 --> 01:12:09,450
Regrets? Things I wish I did?

1558
01:12:09,533 --> 01:12:11,368
I do have a lot of regrets,

1559
01:12:11,869 --> 01:12:14,538
but in terms of doing something more…

1560
01:12:15,247 --> 01:12:17,249
I feel like I have been really honest, so…

1561
01:12:17,333 --> 01:12:18,375
You feel satisfied?

1562
01:12:19,168 --> 01:12:20,961
- I agree.
- In the past,

1563
01:12:21,045 --> 01:12:22,546
I always used to hide my feelings.

1564
01:12:22,629 --> 01:12:24,715
But since coming here,
I've been a bit too direct.

1565
01:12:25,382 --> 01:12:27,843
But it seemed so natural,
as if that's just your personality.

1566
01:12:27,926 --> 01:12:29,094
The way you speak too…

1567
01:12:29,595 --> 01:12:31,263
It didn't seem out of character for you.

1568
01:12:31,347 --> 01:12:33,974
After my date with you, I told the girls

1569
01:12:34,058 --> 01:12:38,354
that I came onto you quite aggressively.

1570
01:12:38,979 --> 01:12:40,022
But then two days later,

1571
01:12:40,105 --> 01:12:43,150
I was like, "He's not into me at all."

1572
01:12:43,233 --> 01:12:44,943
And so…

1573
01:12:45,027 --> 01:12:47,112
I embarrassed myself crying on TV

1574
01:12:47,196 --> 01:12:48,030
- because of you.
- I'm sorry.

1575
01:12:49,198 --> 01:12:50,366
I'm sorry for a lot of things.

1576
01:12:53,577 --> 01:12:56,622
One of the things I feel
sorry about and regret is…

1577
01:12:58,540 --> 01:13:02,378
I know it's late,
but I'm finally starting to see you.

1578
01:13:02,461 --> 01:13:04,088
- He's noticing Han-ju?
- He is?

1579
01:13:04,171 --> 01:13:05,839
Does he finally see her charm?

1580
01:13:05,923 --> 01:13:07,424
- That's so great.
- Yeah.

1581
01:13:07,508 --> 01:13:10,677
This season is really… It's great.

1582
01:13:11,970 --> 01:13:12,971
So…

1583
01:13:13,764 --> 01:13:15,474
What? You little…

1584
01:13:16,100 --> 01:13:17,017
I'm sorry.

1585
01:13:18,018 --> 01:13:20,521
I've started noticing you
now that I have the headspace.

1586
01:13:21,438 --> 01:13:23,732
This is so annoying.
How am I supposed to take this?

1587
01:13:24,775 --> 01:13:26,151
Oh, man. What am I…

1588
01:13:27,945 --> 01:13:29,196
I don't know what I'm saying.

1589
01:13:29,822 --> 01:13:30,948
Anyway, yeah…

1590
01:13:33,534 --> 01:13:34,493
Anyway,

1591
01:13:35,202 --> 01:13:37,663
I don't know how big
your interest in me is, but…

1592
01:13:40,457 --> 01:13:42,626
You're the first person
to tell me I'm handsome.

1593
01:13:43,210 --> 01:13:45,421
- You <i>are</i> handsome.
- Thanks.

1594
01:13:45,504 --> 01:13:46,547
I really…

1595
01:13:47,631 --> 01:13:48,465
I appreciate it.

1596
01:13:51,802 --> 01:13:53,512
- It's cold, right? Shall we head back?
- Let's go.

1597
01:13:54,388 --> 01:13:56,181
Thanks for talking to me like this.

1598
01:13:59,059 --> 01:14:03,063
I realized I hadn't been
totally delusional,

1599
01:14:03,647 --> 01:14:08,527
<i>so it made me think that maybe</i>
<i>I shouldn't give up hope just yet.</i>

1600
01:14:10,988 --> 01:14:14,283
- Jin-woo seems interested in her.
- Yeah.

1601
01:14:14,366 --> 01:14:15,492
I think so too.

1602
01:14:15,576 --> 01:14:17,703
Because Jin-woo is getting

1603
01:14:17,786 --> 01:14:20,956
- a bit tired of waiting for Jeong-eun.
- He is.

1604
01:14:21,039 --> 01:14:25,377
But he's realizing now
that Han-ju's been really good to him,

1605
01:14:25,461 --> 01:14:27,337
and she's consistently
shown her interest in him.

1606
01:14:27,421 --> 01:14:31,049
But what I liked most about it was

1607
01:14:31,675 --> 01:14:35,304
that Han-ju was genuinely
happy and smiling.

1608
01:14:35,387 --> 01:14:37,848
- That's enough for me.
- Yeah.

1609
01:14:37,931 --> 01:14:42,060
But why are we seeing
so many new couples this close to the end?

1610
01:14:42,144 --> 01:14:45,147
- At this rate, our Ms. Popular,
- What's going to happen?

1611
01:14:45,230 --> 01:14:47,524
Su-ji, might end up alone…

1612
01:14:47,608 --> 01:14:48,567
It's looking that way.

1613
01:14:48,650 --> 01:14:52,029
…while everyone else happily couples up.

1614
01:14:52,112 --> 01:14:53,238
- Yeah.
- It's possible.

1615
01:14:53,322 --> 01:14:56,617
- We basically have two new couples.
- We do.

1616
01:14:57,117 --> 01:14:59,745
ETERNAL SINGLES' POST OFFICE

1617
01:15:02,581 --> 01:15:04,333
I'd better hurry and get her a gift.

1618
01:15:04,416 --> 01:15:05,584
<i>A gift?</i>

1619
01:15:07,044 --> 01:15:08,378
Is it this?

1620
01:15:09,129 --> 01:15:10,714
Tangerine card holder…

1621
01:15:11,632 --> 01:15:12,758
This is it.

1622
01:15:14,968 --> 01:15:18,013
<i>I used my remaining gift coupons</i>
<i>on Hyun-seo.</i>

1623
01:15:18,096 --> 01:15:19,973
- Yes. Use them all.
- Great.

1624
01:15:20,057 --> 01:15:23,018
- He used them on Hyun-seo. Good.
- It's all for her.

1625
01:15:23,101 --> 01:15:25,604
We played the Truth Game,
and one of the questions was…

1626
01:15:25,687 --> 01:15:28,815
- "Something you want from your top pick."
- "Something you want."

1627
01:15:28,899 --> 01:15:29,942
Something I want?

1628
01:15:31,485 --> 01:15:34,696
Give me the tangerine card holder
in the Post Office as a gift.

1629
01:15:37,282 --> 01:15:38,992
She gave an order.

1630
01:15:39,076 --> 01:15:40,869
She sounded like a boss.

1631
01:15:40,953 --> 01:15:44,998
<i>She said she wanted to get</i>
<i>the tangerine card holder from someone.</i>

1632
01:15:45,082 --> 01:15:47,751
<i>So I ran to the Post Office</i>
<i>as soon as the group split up,</i>

1633
01:15:47,834 --> 01:15:49,127
<i>in case someone else got to it first.</i>

1634
01:15:49,211 --> 01:15:50,546
<i>I bought that first.</i>

1635
01:15:51,588 --> 01:15:53,632
<i>- That was close.</i>
<i>- He's in a rush.</i>

1636
01:15:53,715 --> 01:15:54,550
<i>In addition to it,</i>

1637
01:15:54,633 --> 01:15:59,513
<i>I wanted her to have</i>
<i>a memorabilia of Jeju Island.</i>

1638
01:15:59,596 --> 01:16:02,432
<i>There was a Jeju Island pen set,</i>

1639
01:16:02,516 --> 01:16:04,685
<i>so I got her that too,</i>
<i>along with a letter.</i>

1640
01:16:06,979 --> 01:16:07,813
All done.

1641
01:16:08,689 --> 01:16:11,733
<i>I used all my three coupons on her.</i>

1642
01:16:11,817 --> 01:16:14,945
I wanted my gifts

1643
01:16:15,529 --> 01:16:19,199
to be sincere and meaningful,
so I only got gifts for her.

1644
01:16:19,283 --> 01:16:20,826
Well done, Hyuk-joon.

1645
01:16:21,410 --> 01:16:22,786
He's come back.

1646
01:16:23,620 --> 01:16:25,247
We thought you'd gone back to your room.

1647
01:16:25,330 --> 01:16:26,915
Oh, right.

1648
01:16:27,916 --> 01:16:31,086
- They all left to their rooms looking sad.
- How come?

1649
01:16:31,587 --> 01:16:33,213
We asked if they wanted to play Mafia,

1650
01:16:33,297 --> 01:16:35,632
but they said they were leaving
with sad voices.

1651
01:16:35,716 --> 01:16:37,301
We got rejected.

1652
01:16:40,846 --> 01:16:42,139
Check your cabinet.

1653
01:16:47,311 --> 01:16:49,229
- He's a funny guy.
- Hyun-seo's so calm.

1654
01:16:49,313 --> 01:16:50,522
He's funny.

1655
01:16:51,398 --> 01:16:52,858
Check your cabinet.

1656
01:17:07,873 --> 01:17:12,419
<i>I was happy to get the card holder</i>
<i>since I'd said I wanted it.</i>

1657
01:17:12,502 --> 01:17:13,837
It's cute.

1658
01:17:15,255 --> 01:17:18,300
He's like a well-trained puppy.

1659
01:17:18,383 --> 01:17:19,259
A puppy?

1660
01:17:20,052 --> 01:17:22,012
- Hyun-seo's quick to forget.
- Yes.

1661
01:17:22,095 --> 01:17:23,347
- She moves on quickly.
- Yeah.

1662
01:17:23,430 --> 01:17:24,848
They're compatible that way.

1663
01:17:26,183 --> 01:17:27,309
HAN SU-JI
AN JEONG-EUN

1664
01:17:27,392 --> 01:17:30,520
<i>I wanted to tell someone so badly,</i>
<i>but since it's meant to be a secret…</i>

1665
01:17:31,104 --> 01:17:32,272
She's in real trouble.

1666
01:17:32,356 --> 01:17:34,941
Yeah, Su-ji seems very troubled right now.

1667
01:17:35,817 --> 01:17:37,152
Did you have fun, at least?

1668
01:17:41,114 --> 01:17:42,741
My head is filled with thoughts.

1669
01:17:44,576 --> 01:17:46,536
Do you not regret not requesting a date?

1670
01:17:47,162 --> 01:17:48,080
I don't know.

1671
01:17:48,163 --> 01:17:49,164
But…

1672
01:17:50,123 --> 01:17:51,833
I don't feel like, "I wish I did it."

1673
01:17:53,710 --> 01:17:56,838
I just suddenly feel like
it might have been a good idea.

1674
01:17:58,382 --> 01:17:59,216
THIS MORNING

1675
01:17:59,299 --> 01:18:00,634
Will you request a date?

1676
01:18:01,301 --> 01:18:03,053
- I don't think so.
- Same.

1677
01:18:06,390 --> 01:18:08,100
Whatever. I'm not picking anyone.

1678
01:18:08,892 --> 01:18:10,060
<i>She felt too conflicted.</i>

1679
01:18:10,143 --> 01:18:13,063
Is there someone you wanted to pick

1680
01:18:13,146 --> 01:18:14,398
but didn't?

1681
01:18:15,023 --> 01:18:18,151
No, I really didn't want
to go on a date with anyone.

1682
01:18:19,569 --> 01:18:22,155
But I feel like I wasted a whole day.

1683
01:18:22,239 --> 01:18:24,908
- Did today feel a bit meaningless?
- Yeah.

1684
01:18:24,991 --> 01:18:27,160
- It makes sense you feel that way.
- Yeah.

1685
01:18:28,078 --> 01:18:32,332
Maybe I should have
made better use of my time.

1686
01:18:32,416 --> 01:18:34,584
Maybe I should have picked someone.

1687
01:18:35,210 --> 01:18:37,546
A lot's on my mind because of that.

1688
01:18:39,965 --> 01:18:43,135
I don't know if it's because things
changed so much yesterday,

1689
01:18:43,218 --> 01:18:45,721
<i>but I felt really conflicted this morning.</i>

1690
01:18:45,804 --> 01:18:48,640
<i>So I didn't want to go on any dates.</i>

1691
01:18:48,724 --> 01:18:53,061
<i>In the tangerine field this morning,</i>
<i>I didn't feel excited at all.</i>

1692
01:18:53,145 --> 01:18:57,357
I felt really troubled
because there are only two days left.

1693
01:18:57,441 --> 01:18:59,151
<i>And then…</i>

1694
01:18:59,234 --> 01:19:00,944
<i>I started thinking about Hyuk-joon.</i>

1695
01:19:01,027 --> 01:19:03,113
<i>He must have gone on a date</i>
<i>with someone else.</i>

1696
01:19:03,196 --> 01:19:05,157
<i>And I started to feel a bit regretful.</i>

1697
01:19:05,240 --> 01:19:06,783
<i>Maybe I should have just given it a shot.</i>

1698
01:19:06,867 --> 01:19:10,829
<i>Requesting a date isn't like</i>
<i>asking him to marry me.</i>

1699
01:19:10,912 --> 01:19:13,623
<i>So why did I make such a big deal of it?</i>

1700
01:19:13,707 --> 01:19:15,625
It just weighed on my mind all day.

1701
01:19:16,126 --> 01:19:18,795
I thought, "Do I really like him?"

1702
01:19:18,879 --> 01:19:21,465
<i>Then, when I got back to the village,</i>

1703
01:19:21,548 --> 01:19:24,134
<i>while I was sitting in the Lounge,</i>

1704
01:19:24,217 --> 01:19:28,513
<i>I found myself noticing</i>
<i>Hyuk-joon whenever he walked past.</i>

1705
01:19:28,597 --> 01:19:31,141
I felt like this had to be
a sign that I was interested.

1706
01:19:31,224 --> 01:19:33,435
That must be why I noticed him

1707
01:19:33,518 --> 01:19:36,146
because I wasn't that bothered
about anyone else.

1708
01:19:36,229 --> 01:19:40,358
I noticed myself paying attention to him.

1709
01:19:41,067 --> 01:19:42,819
<i>I just have a lot on my mind.</i>

1710
01:19:42,903 --> 01:19:44,613
She should've requested
a date with Hyuk-joon.

1711
01:19:44,696 --> 01:19:48,116
That could've helped her figure out
her feelings more clearly.

1712
01:19:48,200 --> 01:19:50,786
I think that deep down,

1713
01:19:50,869 --> 01:19:54,080
Su-ji was probably hoping
Hyuk-joon might request a date with her.

1714
01:19:54,164 --> 01:19:55,665
I think she definitely did

1715
01:19:55,749 --> 01:19:59,044
because when you like someone,
you get your hopes up.

1716
01:19:59,127 --> 01:20:01,046
- That's true.
- So I think

1717
01:20:01,129 --> 01:20:05,759
she strongly hoped that Hyuk-joon
would request a date with her.

1718
01:20:05,842 --> 01:20:08,678
And that's what she probably meant
by leaving it up to fate.

1719
01:20:09,846 --> 01:20:11,640
Do you want to drop by the Post Office?

1720
01:20:11,723 --> 01:20:13,517
- Sure.
- I just want to quickly check

1721
01:20:13,600 --> 01:20:14,893
if I got anything.

1722
01:20:16,520 --> 01:20:18,188
Right now…

1723
01:20:19,022 --> 01:20:21,066
Up until now,

1724
01:20:21,149 --> 01:20:24,402
I felt like giving a gift was a big deal,

1725
01:20:24,486 --> 01:20:26,363
so I didn't want to give a gift to anyone.

1726
01:20:26,446 --> 01:20:28,990
But I kind of want to give
a gift as a lighthearted gesture.

1727
01:20:29,950 --> 01:20:32,160
She shouldn't think of it
as such a big deal.

1728
01:20:52,556 --> 01:20:53,807
He's checking if she took it.

1729
01:20:54,808 --> 01:20:56,268
She took it.

1730
01:21:09,781 --> 01:21:12,450
CHOI HYUK-JOON

1731
01:21:18,081 --> 01:21:19,541
He got something.

1732
01:21:19,624 --> 01:21:20,917
Wait, who is it from?

1733
01:21:27,382 --> 01:21:28,675
<i>I got gloves.</i>

1734
01:21:28,758 --> 01:21:29,759
Hold on.

1735
01:21:30,260 --> 01:21:31,720
No!

1736
01:21:31,803 --> 01:21:32,804
Who gave them?

1737
01:21:32,888 --> 01:21:35,390
Hyuk-joon is going to get swayed again.

1738
01:21:35,473 --> 01:21:37,684
A gift is a huge deal to him.

1739
01:21:40,270 --> 01:21:43,899
I think I'm just going to tell Hyuk-joon.

1740
01:21:43,982 --> 01:21:44,816
Tell him what?

1741
01:21:44,900 --> 01:21:48,820
That I don't know what this feeling is,
but I've been noticing him.

1742
01:22:50,882 --> 01:22:52,884
Subtitle translation by: Hannah Og Nam
